{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition","id":1224340,"title":"Ask a question, get an answer: Scion Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-03T06:35:28-07:00","id":1224340,"title":"Ask a question, get an answer: Scion Edition","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> mentioned they hadn't seen an 'Ask a Question' thread for Scion, so I decided to create one.<br /> <br /> This thread is for Scion questions which don't require a thread to themselves, and which only need answers from other Scion players/STs/Storyguides.<br /> <br /> Questions can be for 1e or 2e, but clearly mark which edition you're asking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T07:11:04-07:00","id":1224352,"title":"","content":"Do we still have cases of Mantles as \u201ctwo gods, but they were identified as the same so they\u2019re Mantles of the same god,\u201d or are Mantles something more like Apollo having the Mantle of Phoebus? (I only skimmed through existing previews due to time constraints, so point me out if they already imply something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T07:29:34-07:00","id":1224357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1224352#post1224352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we still have cases of Mantles as \u201ctwo gods, but they were identified as the same so they\u2019re Mantles of the same god,\u201d or are Mantles something more like Apollo having the Mantle of Phoebus? (I only skimmed through existing previews due to time constraints, so point me out if they already imply something.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Mantle is a Specific Divine Identity... Ares and Mars are two Mantles currently being worn by the same God... Yama, on the other hand, is a member of 4 different Pantheons and has no separate Mantles since he's basically the same guy in each. The Shen have merged Mantles and given them to the same person for administrative purposes. The Orisha of Yoruba and the Goddesses of Hinduism constantly shift and borrow each other's Mantles as a matter of course. From what we know so far, a Mantle is a construct within Fate, built of Legend, and can move from person to person... You can, technically, literally become Zeus by stealing his Mantle for yourself.<br /> <br /> Apollo being Phoebus is, on my opinion, more an example of a Title, which is a seperate thing entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T07:54:33-07:00","id":1224690,"title":"","content":"A question on the Dream virtue for the Manitou. Exactly what type of behavior is it trying to encourage and how does it becomes in conflict with Pride? That is something that i was unclear of after reading their previews.<br /> <br /> Also how strong can a Sorcerer can get? As the Orisha's normal antagonists would be them I'm curious on how that would work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T09:53:07-07:00","id":1224730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1224352#post1224352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we still have cases of Mantles as \u201ctwo gods, but they were identified as the same so they\u2019re Mantles of the same god,\u201d or are Mantles something more like Apollo having the Mantle of Phoebus? (I only skimmed through existing previews due to time constraints, so point me out if they already imply something.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's actually a nice little chunk of info on Mantles in the Companion outline that Neal so graciously shared with the latest <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/scion-2nd-edition-tabletop-rpg/posts/2204557\" target=\"_blank\"> ks update</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T01:28:48-07:00","id":1226394,"title":"","content":"OK so I have a question. <br /> <br /> Actually, it a question from a friend that I was kinda giving the Scion 2E blurb to and realized I did not know the answer.<br /> <br /> Sorry if this has been answered elsewhere, I've not trawled through the forums nearly enough. <br /> <br /> So from what I understand the general premise of Scion 2E is that the supernatural is an accepted part of the modern world. There is no masquerade. In addition, all these old pagan faiths never died out and modern day paganism is not a reconstructed religion but actually has a mostly continuous history. <br /> <br /> Am I also right in saying that, in broad strokes, the last couple of thousands of years of human history roughly matches that of our own world? <br /> <br /> If both of these are true then the following question got asked:<br /> <br /> How is this the case? Considering that a huge number of historical social and religious trends in the last couple of thousands years kinda rely on Christianities predominance of at least Europe and via that several other parts of the world during the age of exploration? <br /> <br /> For an example, the many, many religious schism in Christianity over that period seem less likely to happen if that religion was facing several other competing religions during say...the dark ages. Especially when said competing religions have Gods that actually get involved in things directly sometimes or at least send powerful proxies to do their bidding. <br /> <br /> Basically, have I missed something about the games pitch or setting that kinda explains this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T02:12:33-07:00","id":1226401,"title":"","content":"Yes, Scion works on the premise that the mythic is a known thing, since a Masquerade would be completely antithetical to the basic feel of the genre that Scion is trying to emulate i.e. mythology, where gods are usually not known for trying to hide their presence from mortals. That being said, most of the World knows about the mythic the way you and I know about organised crime... We know it exists, we may have some wild ideas about how it actually works stemming from pop culture, we may think it'd be really cool to meet one, or that their not worth the hype... But by and large most of us will go out entire lives without knowingly meeting anyone from that Sphere.<br /> <br /> In addition, while a most of the religions that were popular in ancient times continue unbroken, the Abrahamic religions are still the dominant religions of the World, and many people, just like in the real World, don't find anything particularly contradictory in going to church and also invoking Jove.<br /> <br /> The history of the World remains largely the same, true, but there are subtle differences in the way people's lives go about... The central conceit of the setting exists to facilitate mythic gameplay, which is the primary point.<br /> <br /> As another point, why would you think the Abrahamic God didn't get involved in his people's history? Sure the other Pantheons have Gods, so do they... It is not too much of a stretch to imagine that they neutralized each other from doing anything greatly flashy and changing the course of history too broadly.<br /> <br /> Finally, Gods don't need worship... Some of them like it, some demand it, some like the Orisha will happily tell you that they're not gods on the first place, but none of them need it... So the idea that the old Pantheons would get up in arms and persecute and stop every single human that converted in order to not lose worshippers is not really something that has reason for happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T09:12:51-07:00","id":1226476,"title":"","content":"Also of note, the Gods weren't always active in The World. Due to the vagaries of Fate and Fate-binding, they apply a lighter touch to interacting with The World, if at all.<br /> <br /> While it doesn't answer every question, the Religions and Cults section on page 24 of Origins sets up good guidelines for how these things unfolded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T09:48:17-07:00","id":1226487,"title":"","content":"The explanation, broadly speaking, is &quot;this is our big ask. This is how it is - now we can backfill to decide how.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T20:19:36-07:00","id":1226654,"title":"","content":"Do Hero-tier denizens PCs that aren't scions still get purviews at character creation? The game says they're playable, but I can't see any text describing whether they can pantheon purviews or if they can start with any fitting purview since they lack a divine parent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T04:07:17-07:00","id":1227997,"title":"","content":"So the section on converting Origin characters to hero (for both scions and denisens ), says give them purviews as described in part 6, part 6 however only describes things for scions so i would say whatever purview seems fitting,<br /> <br /> my question is can the legendary creature paths in hero be used in an Origin level game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12845,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","user":"ahather","date":".  Oops i was being obtuse. 06-18-2018, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T10:56:34-07:00","id":1228626,"title":"","content":"I would guess tehy can, but should not, mostly due to power balance, but I didnt read them through very carefully, so I might be talking nonsense. But would explain why the Scion Origin have fewer Legendary Paths than Hero, as creatures are usually quite stronger than a pre-visitation Scion would be.<br /> <br /> By the way, my two doubts.<br /> <br /> Maybe someone already answered, but how does defense for players works? For monster I get it, a fix ammount of extra success needed. Easy. But it says players can choose their way of defending on the turn (which I imagine is something like rolling away or blocking or parrying) but doesnt say which skill to use. Is it Athletics (Dexterity)?<br /> <br /> Second, but not least important, does Scions on Hero have less Skill points than Scion on Origin? Asking because in the character creation on Origin, on the final steps, there says the get 5 extra skill points to distribute as they wish, but says nothing on the Hero creation chart.<br /> <br /> I believe those are two mistakes that will be fixed on the final product, but planning a game to this July. Thanks in advance to everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T14:40:03-07:00","id":1228681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1228626#post1228626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would guess tehy can, but should not, mostly due to power balance, but I didnt read them through very carefully, so I might be talking nonsense. But would explain why the Scion Origin have fewer Legendary Paths than Hero, as creatures are usually quite stronger than a pre-visitation Scion would be.<br /> <br /> By the way, my two doubts.<br /> <br /> Maybe someone already answered, but how does defense for players works? For monster I get it, a fix ammount of extra success needed. Easy. But it says players can choose their way of defending on the turn (which I imagine is something like rolling away or blocking or parrying) but doesnt say which skill to use. Is it Athletics (Dexterity)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Defense for PCs is a pool of your highest Resilience Attribute. Stamina, Composure, or Resolve.<br /> <br /> When you first get attacked in a round, you roll your Defend pool. You can spend your successes on Defense stunts, such as &quot;Dive for cover&quot; or just to boost your defense.<br /> <br /> For the purposes of defense calculations, Neall confirmed that your Defense starts at 1 and can be boosted with successes. But don't underestimate blowing some successes on diving for cover. Cover gives bonus health levels to soak an incoming attack, not unlike Hard Armor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, but not least important, does Scions on Hero have less Skill points than Scion on Origin? Asking because in the character creation on Origin, on the final steps, there says the get 5 extra skill points to distribute as they wish, but says nothing on the Hero creation chart. </div> </div> </div>Ah, that's some wires crossed when Neall was writing the Hero Chargen. Heroes should get all the bonuses when freshly created that an Origin character should. The bonus skill points, the extra attribute dot, the choice of two additional Knacks or four extra dots of Birthright<br /> <br /> Edit: Now's probably a good point to link <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1etYiuHfHR-nTI5obsKhL44stbRmLkuvw2Z6qae_lbWM/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. It's an FAQ of questions I've seen answered on the Scion Discord, each answered by Neall himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 06-19-2018, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T15:49:39-07:00","id":1228990,"title":"","content":"If you have choose to have the 4 dots of Birthrights at Origin, is it possible to gain access to a Purview, then? With just the innate power and a motif?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5619-starkjunior","name":"StarkJunior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T11:49:58-07:00","id":1229189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StarkJunior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1228990#post1228990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have choose to have the 4 dots of Birthrights at Origin, is it possible to gain access to a Purview, then? With just the innate power and a motif?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that beings without Legend don't get Purview Access, including the Innate powers. Some Sorcerers can weave Marvels but even they need to steal the power to do so","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T13:24:11-07:00","id":1229208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1229189#post1229189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure that beings without Legend don't get Purview Access, including the Innate powers. Some Sorcerers can weave Marvels but even they need to steal the power to do so</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, alright, so it'd just be you have the Relic and the non-Purview things until Hero, I imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5619-starkjunior","name":"StarkJunior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T14:23:10-07:00","id":1229230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StarkJunior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1229208#post1229208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, alright, so it'd just be you have the Relic and the non-Purview things until Hero, I imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Relics can give you Knacks and Enhancement. Those are invaluable.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually that's something to note in general about 2e. I've seen a lot of people talking about Purviews and Boons like they're the be-all of being a Scion. In reality, Knacks will be your workhorses. You're not gonna be spamming Boons every round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 06-21-2018, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T15:35:16-07:00","id":1229245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1229230#post1229230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Relics can give you Knacks and Enhancement. Those are invaluable.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually that's something to note in general about 2e. I've seen a lot of people talking about Purviews and Boons like they're the be-all of being a Scion. In reality, Knacks will be your workhorses. You're not gonna be spamming Boons every round.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, for sure - I just wanted to be super clear with Birthrights at Origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5619-starkjunior","name":"StarkJunior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T00:05:20-07:00","id":1229536,"title":"","content":"Say I have a Relic Trumpet that gives Artistry (Music) and Chaos.<br /> <br /> That Relic comes with the Motif (Steal the show) that limits how it can be used.<br /> <br /> Does the Relic's Motif dictate the Motif you get for specializing in a Purview? Or do I also have to choose another Motif for when using the trumpet to perform Fire or Beast marvels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1178-ravenmancer","user":"Ravenmancer","date":". 06-23-2018, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1178-ravenmancer","name":"Ravenmancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T06:59:10-07:00","id":1229586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravenmancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1229536#post1229536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say I have a Relic Trumpet that gives Artistry (Music) and Chaos.<br /> <br /> That Relic comes with the Motif (Steal the show) that limits how it can be used.<br /> <br /> Does the Relic's Motif dictate the Motif you get for specializing in a Purview? Or do I also have to choose another Motif for when using the trumpet to perform Fire or Beast marvels?</div> </div> </div> </div>You get two Motifs, one from the Relic that can only be used for Purviews channeled through that Relic, and one for specialization that that can be used for any Purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T12:38:32-07:00","id":1229637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1229586#post1229586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You get two Motifs, one from the Relic that can only be used for Purviews channeled through that Relic, and one for specialization that that can be used for any Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if I wanted to perform a Fire marvel through my Artistry (Music) granted Motif, would it also have to fit within the Trumpet's Motif?<br /> <br /> At least up until Demigod(?) where I can supposedly gain additional innate purviews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1178-ravenmancer","name":"Ravenmancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T13:21:38-07:00","id":1229642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravenmancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1229637#post1229637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if I wanted to perform a Fire marvel through my Artistry (Music) granted Motif, would it also have to fit within the Trumpet's Motif?<br /> <br /> At least up until Demigod(?) where I can supposedly gain additional innate purviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it would not, only the Artistry (Music) specific Motif. Say if your Relic Motif is Steal the Show, and your Specialization Motif is Music Makes the World Go Round, your Fire Marvel would have to be inline with the second, not the first.<br /> <br /> We don't know yet if Demigod gives you additional Innates, though you can always use your Pantheon granted Motif for any Purview you have access to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T22:17:06-07:00","id":1229743,"title":"","content":"Don't know if this has been asked before, but what is a Feat of Scale? Its mentioned a lot, I understand what Feats are and what Scale is but what is a Feat of Scale specifically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2553-kai","name":"Kai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2553_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T03:29:28-07:00","id":1229773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1229743#post1229743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't know if this has been asked before, but what is a Feat of Scale? Its mentioned a lot, I understand what Feats are and what Scale is but what is a Feat of Scale specifically?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are various ways in which you can turn an action into a Feat of Scale. Once you do this, your effective Scale for that Action increases by your Legend/2 (rounding up). This stacks with any Scale you might have from other sources, for example, the Epic Strength Innate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T21:23:36-07:00","id":1230459,"title":"","content":"Just want reconfirmation because I forgot whether it's a thing or not. But Titans who only contain access to one Purview compared to Gods but in that Purview they are more powerful to what the Gods can do through sheer specialization thus makes them more equal to ones with the same legend score.<br /> <br /> Also can Titans be Primodials that is be super large they can't leave Overworlds or is there has to be a seperation between the two. Ia rhis better for the ask neall thread","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 06-27-2018, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T22:02:33-07:00","id":1230463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1230459#post1230459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just want reconfirmation because I forgot whether it's a think or not. But Titans who only contain access to one Purview compared to Gods but in that Purview they are more powerful to what the Gods can do through sheer specialization thus makes them more equal to ones with the same legend score.<br /> <br /> Also can Titans be Primodials that is be super large they can't leave Overworlds or is there has to be a seperation between the two. Ia rhis better for the ask neall thread</div> </div> </div> </div>Titans can have more than one Purview, though they are usually narrowly focused. They are also not necessarily any more powerful in that Purview than Gods are... it would be a little weird to say that Agni is less the master of Fire than Kagutsuchi. And Neall has stated earlier that &quot;Gods <i>are</i> their Purviews, in a very real way&quot;. So the difference between Gods and Titans is not how much power they have over their Purviews, but in how much power their Purviews have over them.<br /> <br /> God Titan and Primordial are different categories of Deities, so the short answer to your second question is, No, they can't... at the same time. But those categories are not fixed and static, and you can absolutely have a Titan become a Primordial... they would just then be a Primordial, not a Titan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T15:24:32-07:00","id":1230656,"title":"","content":"Alright so this just came up;<br /> <br /> I've got a guy wanting to play a Werewolf/Scion of Loki/Incarnation of Fenris.<br /> <br /> No problem, the game is designed with that as a possibility. Origin Werewolf, Werewolf as one of his callings, take Lycanthropy as one of his starting Knacks....<br /> <br /> It also lists Vulnerability (Silver) and Imperfect Disguise as Werewolf Knacks.<br /> <br /> Is there some hidden benefit for taking either of those that I'm just not seeing? Or do you get them automatically just for being a werewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1178-ravenmancer","name":"Ravenmancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T21:56:13-07:00","id":1231526,"title":"","content":"In hero it says:<br /> <br /> &quot;Characters begin play with five Knacks from their Callings, one for each Calling dot a character begins with. One Knack may be swapped out for another during a minor milestone. Additional Knacks may be purchased with Experience, but a character may only have five Knacks \u201cactive\u201d at a time, corresponding to their Calling dots, until they gain more by rising in Legend. Immortal Knacks are worth two Calling dots to keep active; thus, a Scion with a Warrior Calling of 4 can have two Immortal Knacks, four Heroic Knacks, or two Heroic and one Immortal Knack active at a time.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does that mean that you can swap it out for one you know as in the &quot;Tweaks&quot; rules in origin or is this a full exchange? If the latter, what is the point of buying knacks more than your callings if you can swap em out anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2553-kai","name":"Kai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2553_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T22:25:21-07:00","id":1231530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1231526#post1231526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In hero it says:<br /> <br /> &quot;Characters begin play with five Knacks from their Callings, one for each Calling dot a character begins with. One Knack may be swapped out for another during a minor milestone. Additional Knacks may be purchased with Experience, but a character may only have five Knacks \u201cactive\u201d at a time, corresponding to their Calling dots, until they gain more by rising in Legend. Immortal Knacks are worth two Calling dots to keep active; thus, a Scion with a Warrior Calling of 4 can have two Immortal Knacks, four Heroic Knacks, or two Heroic and one Immortal Knack active at a time.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does that mean that you can swap it out for one you know as in the &quot;Tweaks&quot; rules in origin or is this a full exchange? If the latter, what is the point of buying knacks more than your callings if you can swap em out anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Tweak... you have to actually have the Knack bought to swap it in. You essentially have a Suite of Knacks from which to choose your current loadout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T09:43:37-07:00","id":1231851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravenmancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1230656#post1230656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright so this just came up;<br /> <br /> I've got a guy wanting to play a Werewolf/Scion of Loki/Incarnation of Fenris.<br /> <br /> No problem, the game is designed with that as a possibility. Origin Werewolf, Werewolf as one of his callings, take Lycanthropy as one of his starting Knacks....<br /> <br /> It also lists Vulnerability (Silver) and Imperfect Disguise as Werewolf Knacks.<br /> <br /> Is there some hidden benefit for taking either of those that I'm just not seeing? Or do you get them automatically just for being a werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Denizens are getting a rework to make it more clear. Most of not all Denizen paths are going to have a persistent condition of sorts that give momentum when they inconvenience you. Like the Kitsune Tail or the Werewolf Silver vulnerability","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T01:22:45-07:00","id":1232575,"title":"","content":"I have a question about things like how do you deal with things that Art, Crafts, Performance and Expression used to handle? I've looked and I can't find anything for what roll you would use to dance, cook a meal, paint a masterpiece, create a song, play an instrument.<br /> <br /> I see in both Academics and Culture that you are exposed to these things and may even study them but being an art critic isn't the same as being able make art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T06:00:45-07:00","id":1232601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1232575#post1232575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about things like how do you deal with things that Art, Crafts, Performance and Expression used to handle? I've looked and I can't find anything for what roll you would use to dance, cook a meal, paint a masterpiece, create a song, play an instrument.<br /> <br /> I see in both Academics and Culture that you are exposed to these things and may even study them but being an art critic isn't the same as being able make art.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things like that are handled through the crafting system and your Paths... It's designed to mostly do away with having to roll things to make stuff... If you have the appropriate Path to paint, and the Skill to represent your knowledge (Culture for formal techniques, Persuasion or Empathy for more free spirited work, Integrity for meditative pieces) you can make the art. The things you actually need to worry about are things like procuring the assets, booking a stage... Etc, that is, things that actually cause Things to happen in game, instead of having your crafter be holed up in his studio painting while others are having adventures, as such tends to not be the best activity in a cooperative game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T11:09:39-07:00","id":1233225,"title":"","content":"What happens when, theoretically speaking, one deity of one pantheon and another deity of a different pantheon produce a child together?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T12:48:46-07:00","id":1233248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1233225#post1233225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when, theoretically speaking, one deity of one pantheon and another deity of a different pantheon produce a child together?</div> </div> </div> </div>The child is Born as a Legend 1 Scion and inherits powers from whichever Parent Visits them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T14:21:46-07:00","id":1233265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1233248#post1233248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The child is Born as a Legend 1 Scion and inherits powers from whichever Parent Visits them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Were I running it at my table, I'd give the Scion (and if they're a PC, they're player) the ability to chose which set of Virtues they want to embrace, and inherit the associated PSP (same of course for being the child of a single god of multiple Pantheons, like the Dharmaraja/Yan Luo/Emma-O... by far the BUSIEST god in the cosmos, given that he's in charge of the managing majority of humanity's souls after death at this point).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T14:41:35-07:00","id":1233276,"title":"","content":"The political implications of an inter-Pantheon pregnancy would definitely be interesting to ponder. <br /> <br /> It probably depends a great deal on how similar the cultures are. If, say, Freya had a fling with Aengus that resulted in a baby, relations between the Aesir and the Tuatha are pretty good. Both cultures have a custom of fosterage, so the kid may even have something of a dual-upbringing between both Pantheons. On the other hand, a child born of, say, Quetzalcoatl and Winonah, whose Pantheons don't get along quite so well? Could be a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":679,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","user":"unnatural1","date":". 07-09-2018, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T08:51:15-07:00","id":1233437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1233265#post1233265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Were I running it at my table, I'd give the Scion (and if they're a PC, they're player) the ability to chose which set of Virtues they want to embrace, and inherit the associated PSP (same of course for being the child of a single god of multiple Pantheons, like the Dharmaraja/Yan Luo/Emma-O... by far the BUSIEST god in the cosmos, given that he's in charge of the managing majority of humanity's souls after death at this point).</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that while he may be in charge, he does have the advantage of getting to use the Shen bureaucracy to delegate...which may have its own problems, but will keep him from being overwhelmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24028-mike-mccall","name":"Mike McCall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T16:29:48-07:00","id":1234437,"title":"","content":"Hello Everybody. I'm having some problems on understanding the Supernatural Path and their Knacks.<br /> <br /> On the Origin says that, if your Supernatural Path grant you access to knacks/birthrights, you need to pay/allocate the points for it as usual. That means you need to pay for the knacks of the path? If yes, with which points? Or you have access to them all, but you still have the limit of 5 active knacks per Session?<br /> <br /> Also, on the Hero book it says that the Denizen dont have boons for free and need to use Marvels to use any power. Does that means that they begin with boon points but still can buy with exp or they cant access it? If I'm right, dont it make them vastly weaker than their Scion counterparts?<br /> <br /> Thanks for the attention, sorry for any trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T19:44:21-07:00","id":1234496,"title":"","content":"Which Pantheon is Columbia part of? Will she still be part of the &quot;American Pantheon&quot; again, or simply treated as a member of the Theoi? For some reason, my brain's been working on a son of Columbia after seeing her name-dropped so much in the Origin book, but I ended up stuck because I didn't know her Pantheon skills or what callings she'd have.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, what happens if a non-scion supernatural entity and a deity (say, for example, a Valkyrie and Tyr) have a child?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T19:59:57-07:00","id":1234500,"title":"","content":"We don\u2019t know yet, but she\u2019ll get a parent/patron blurb in the Companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T23:39:39-07:00","id":1234549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica1000</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1234496#post1234496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On an unrelated note, what happens if a non-scion supernatural entity and a deity (say, for example, a Valkyrie and Tyr) have a child?</div> </div> </div> </div>The child can be a Born Scion, and they have the option to replace a Calling with a Supernatural Path representing their heritage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T10:32:20-07:00","id":1234697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1234437#post1234437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello Everybody. I'm having some problems on understanding the Supernatural Path and their Knacks.<br /> <br /> On the Origin says that, if your Supernatural Path grant you access to knacks/birthrights, you need to pay/allocate the points for it as usual. That means you need to pay for the knacks of the path? If yes, with which points? Or you have access to them all, but you still have the limit of 5 active knacks per Session?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, let's take a Kitsune as an example. At Origin-Tier, you have space for one Knack, which can be a Kitsune Knack.<br /> <br /> If they awaken to their Legend, through deeds or through a Visitation, they have the option to instead of one of 11 standard Callings, this Kitsune can replace one of their three Callings with an effective Kitsune Calling, which can be leveled and ranked like other Callings, and the Knack Slots this Kitsune Calling provides can be used for Kitsune Knacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, on the Hero book it says that the Denizen dont have boons for free and need to use Marvels to use any power. Does that means that they begin with boon points but still can buy with exp or they cant access it? If I'm right, dont it make them vastly weaker than their Scion counterparts? </div> </div> </div>Now I believe it works like this... If a Denizen gains Legend through means <i>other</i> than a Visitation, just growing as a Satyr or a Naga or what have you, then they effectively only have the one Calling, that matches their type, ranked at 5. I believe they can also pick one logical Purview to have access to... But they don't get Boons, and instead use their Legend to power Marvels.<br /> <br /> Now a thing to note here: You can't <i>buy</i> Boons in 2e. The number is fixed.<br /> <br /> And that <i>will</i> make many Denizens somewhat weaker than Scions. They're still viable and many can do specific tricks, but you can also be a Denizen Scion if you're worried about power. Inari, for instance, is the patron of all Kitsune, A Naga may get Chosen by one of the Deva, and I imagine there's a fair number of Amazon Scions who get Chosen by Athena or Artemis.<br /> <br /> Hell, there's a sidebar mentioning that the world is becoming increasingly mixed, culturally. A Satyr can become a Scion of a member of the Kami, or the Shen could draft a werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T17:45:09-07:00","id":1234833,"title":"","content":"hows Mon ey work in Scion or is it considered irrelevant/<br /> <br /> Im pretty sure some Scions at origin, or hero will devote most of their timje acquiring it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T18:03:07-07:00","id":1234839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1234833#post1234833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hows Mon ey work in Scion or is it considered irrelevant/<br /> <br /> Im pretty sure some Scions at origin, or hero will devote most of their timje acquiring it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Path system exists to leverag you background/job/etc for resources you need in-game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T18:42:20-07:00","id":1234844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1234833#post1234833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hows Mon ey work in Scion or is it considered irrelevant/<br /> <br /> Im pretty sure some Scions at origin, or hero will devote most of their timje acquiring it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Insufficients funds could make for a nice social Complication or Condition.<br /> With a persistent condition being like cursed ''to never be able to hold onto wealth'' (maybe with the prosperity purview or the Tuatha D\u00e9 Danaan PSP)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T19:10:51-07:00","id":1234849,"title":"","content":"I still don't fully understand Asset skills. Are they the only skills the scions can have, or just skills that the scion has an advantage on? Neither books are very clear about them, and the guide section mentions that Guides don't grant the +1 given to stunts for normal Asset skills, a rule that I also can't find, so I'm very confused atm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T21:15:21-07:00","id":1234863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica1000</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1234849#post1234849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't fully understand Asset skills. Are they the only skills the scions can have, or just skills that the scion has an advantage on? Neither books are very clear about them, and the guide section mentions that Guides don't grant the +1 given to stunts for normal Asset skills, a rule that I also can't find, so I'm very confused atm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each Pantheon has two Asset Skills. Each Path that you choose has three Skills associated with it... for your Pantheon Path, two of those three Skills must me your Pantheon's Asset Skills... this means that you will always start with at least a single dot in each Skill, even if the Path is tertiary. They don't have any advantage inherently, at least none that all the other Skills bound to your Paths don't have. Also, Guide Asset Skills section doesn't say anything about getting +1 to Stunts, merely the fact that you will automatically start with 1 dot in each... the Guide's Asset Skills are the skills through whose rolls you can access the Guide's Stunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T05:32:15-07:00","id":1234918,"title":"","content":"Are their any reasons you can see to delay visitations for a Chosen or Created Scion? <br /> <br /> Best I can see is to let them return to their human liveves (or start building them) for a bit unsure of everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T08:03:08-07:00","id":1234957,"title":"","content":"So, one thing in Origin seems odd to me. Everywhere else in the rules, range is specified in bands, but in combat stunts, like Close Combat Attack\u2019s Shove and Grapple\u2019s Throw, the outcome is in meters based on Might. Barring a Might Scale coming into effect, this is usually just going to send the person/weapon into the Close range band. But the introduction of meters here when everything else in in range bands is clunky. Surely there\u2019s a better way to measure Shove/Throw outcomes than having to calculate in meters and then convert those into rand bands to stay consistent with the rest of the system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":972,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/972-fairlyhyperman","user":"Fairlyhyperman","date":". 07-14-2018, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/972-fairlyhyperman","name":"Fairlyhyperman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T11:07:40-07:00","id":1235018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1234918#post1234918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are their any reasons you can see to delay visitations for a Chosen or Created Scion?<br /> <br /> Best I can see is to let them return to their human liveves (or start building them) for a bit unsure of everything.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well with the chosen it might be to see how they grow and handle things. Basically the God knows/has decided they'll be a useful tool eventually, but isn't sure how they'll specifically be helpful; or they figure the visitation will draw them too far into The World and and the restrictions of Fate will be more problematic as well as just more dangerous foes going after a post visitation Chosen as opposed to one that hasn't. <br /> <br /> Now the created it would vary on why they were made. A child created for some worshippers of a god in return for certain service or just as a reward might still have the spark to be useful as a Scion, but it wouldn't be as necessary for them to have the divine might that a visitation would allow them access to as one created for the purpose of retrieving a relic from a group of titanspawn.<br /> <br /> Of course there's always the possibility that the god doesn't think they need the power of a Scion that has had the visitation yet. Maybe they're right, maybe they're wrong, that's just what the God has decided for the time being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T12:34:43-07:00","id":1235050,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit confused on the paths in Origin. In it they reference dots and ranks but no where does it say in creating paths you accolate any points in it tho? Is this something that got cut?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T14:08:59-07:00","id":1235080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1235050#post1235050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit confused on the paths in Origin. In it they reference dots and ranks but no where does it say in creating paths you accolate any points in it tho? Is this something that got cut?</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be artifact text. Trinity, which also uses Storypath, does rank your Paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T17:15:05-07:00","id":1235112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1235050#post1235050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit confused on the paths in Origin. In it they reference dots and ranks but no where does it say in creating paths you accolate any points in it tho? Is this something that got cut?</div> </div> </div> </div>Make note of that with a page reference on the Errata thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T03:21:36-07:00","id":1235227,"title":"","content":"Do Kitsune (pp. 163) have some method of shapechanging? They have Mortal Mask but that is only for one mortal form, so it's hardly living up to &quot;Legend&quot; as it were. Perhaps they get more forms as they get points of Legend?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, shouldn't Cu sith have a persistent condition: You're a dog. Woof woof?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T19:55:58-07:00","id":1235403,"title":"","content":"So I've noticed in the origin book for 2nd ed that to see through an illusion the check is &quot;Awareness+Cunning&quot; this was strange because I had a look through the book and it has no other mention of awareness.<br /> <br /> Have I missed some thing? Or is it just not there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24414-sixxodd","name":"SixxOdd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T21:09:08-07:00","id":1235415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixxOdd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1235403#post1235403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've noticed in the origin book for 2nd ed that to see through an illusion the check is &quot;Awareness+Cunning&quot; this was strange because I had a look through the book and it has no other mention of awareness.<br /> <br /> Have I missed some thing? Or is it just not there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as far as I can find either.<br /> <br /> Put it in the errata thread with a page reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T23:26:32-07:00","id":1235459,"title":"","content":"Is there anything stopping a Scion from being a Saint of the Pantheon as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T23:49:17-07:00","id":1235462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixxOdd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1235403#post1235403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've noticed in the origin book for 2nd ed that to see through an illusion the check is &amp;quot;Awareness+Cunning&amp;quot; this was strange because I had a look through the book and it has no other mention of awareness.<br /> <br /> Have I missed some thing? Or is it just not there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially odd as elsewhere in the book it mentions that no there is no Awareness Skill and that this is very deliberate.<br /> <br /> Until this gets corrected I'd recommend allowing players to use the Occult skill to sense whether they're in an illusion, allowing alternate skills for creativity (like Survival to realize that the wolves aren't actually interacting with the foliage around them)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T00:00:34-07:00","id":1235466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1235459#post1235459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything stopping a Scion from being a Saint of the Pantheon as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see what would stop them, though it would probably be more appropriate for those who are Chosen instead of Born. Since all Scions need to take a Virtue track already, you're really just getting access to a couple of Knacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T00:13:13-07:00","id":1235469,"title":"","content":"I'm still confused by what Specialties actually do, when you get them, and what (if any) their Experience cost is. In the sidebar on p. 59, it says that they add a +1 Enhancement bonus on all rolls with that Skill... a nice bonus, especially since it specifically says all rolls with the skill, not just those where the specialty would apply. So any Scion with at least 4 dots in a skill always has a +1 Enhancement bonus on that skill, not just when it would be appropriate to the specialty definition?<br /> <br /> To complicate this, it says in the character creation section on Skills that specialties add a +1 Enhancement skills other than the one it is assigned to if the specialty seems relevant, but doesn't mention either the +1 Enhancement to the skill itself, nor that it grants an extra momentum on failed rolls. As far as I can tell, this cross-Skill bonus to Specialties isn't mentioned anywhere else in the rules (like the section on Enhancements, or the sidebar for Specialties in the Skills section). So is this an artifact from an older version of the rules, or still a valid use for specialties?<br /> <br /> The sidebar in the Skills section also says that they get these Specialties at 4 dots (somewhat implying that it is free), but it says during character creation that you get them at 3 dots. Later, under advancement, it says that specialties cost 3 Experience, which seems to contradict the bit in the Skills section that indicates you get them for free at 4 dots. So do you get them for free when a skill reaches 4, for free at 3 during Character Creation, or for 3 Experiences each regardless of skill level, or some combination?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 07-16-2018, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T00:44:45-07:00","id":1235474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1235466#post1235466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see what would stop them, though it would probably be more appropriate for those who are Chosen instead of Born. Since all Scions need to take a Virtue track already, you're really just getting access to a couple of Knacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the ability to ignore Scale once per session is why I was asking. That is a top tier ability, in my opinion. Though you have to act.... intense... to qualify for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T00:59:42-07:00","id":1235476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1235469#post1235469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still confused by what Specialties actually do, when you get them, and what (if any) their Experience cost is. In the sidebar on p. 59, it says that they add a +1 Enhancement bonus on all rolls with that Skill... a nice bonus, especially since it specifically says all rolls with the skill, not just those where the specialty would apply. So any Scion with at least 4 dots in a skill always has a +1 Enhancement bonus on that skill, not just when it would be appropriate to the specialty definition?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably artifact text from the older version. Specialties at first didn't give Enhancement in their base skills, they instead granted extra Momentum upon a failure, and +1E to cross-skill applications. Such as a Culture check to identify a historically significant sword using your Sword specialty in Close Combat. The whole &quot;They also grant 1E to the base skill&quot; was added later. I'd run it as &quot;If the Specialty applies&quot; and anybody at my table who tried to argue that the Enhancement applies to ALL rolls with the base skill even if the Specialty doesn't apply would get slapped with a fish and told to stop being a putz. (Not literally. I don't have fish to go around)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To complicate this, it says in the character creation section on Skills that specialties add a +1 Enhancement skills other than the one it is assigned to if the specialty seems relevant, but doesn't mention either the +1 Enhancement to the skill itself, nor that it grants an extra momentum on failed rolls. As far as I can tell, this cross-Skill bonus to Specialties isn't mentioned anywhere else in the rules (like the section on Enhancements, or the sidebar for Specialties in the Skills section). So is this an artifact from an older version of the rules, or still a valid use for specialties? </div> </div> </div>To the best of my knowledge, the +1 Cross Skill Enhancement still applies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The sidebar in the Skills section also says that they get these Specialties at 4 dots (somewhat implying that it is free), but it says during character creation that you get them at 3 dots. Later, under advancement, it says that specialties cost 3 Experience, which seems to contradict the bit in the Skills section that indicates you get them for free at 4 dots. So do you get them for free when a skill reaches 4, for free at 3 during Character Creation, or for 3 Experiences each regardless of skill level, or some combination? </div> </div> </div>At my table, I'd say during Chargen you get the Specialty for free at 3+ ranks. In play, if your Skill raises to 4 or higher with experience, free Specialty. And you can buy <i>another</i> Specialty for 3 experience, so if you want to say, have &quot;Desert&quot;, 'Rainforest&quot;, and &quot;Tundra&quot; as Survival Specialties, you'll need to buy at least one Specialty.<br /> <br /> Edit: Though you may want to mention this in the Errata Thread asking for clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T11:32:59-07:00","id":1235651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fairlyhyperman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1234957#post1234957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, one thing in Origin seems odd to me. Everywhere else in the rules, range is specified in bands, but in combat stunts, like Close Combat Attack\u2019s Shove and Grapple\u2019s Throw, the outcome is in meters based on Might. Barring a Might Scale coming into effect, this is usually just going to send the person/weapon into the Close range band. But the introduction of meters here when everything else in in range bands is clunky. Surely there\u2019s a better way to measure Shove/Throw outcomes than having to calculate in meters and then convert those into rand bands to stay consistent with the rest of the system?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? A weakling is still going to drop the guy in Close range if he's trying for a Throw. But just saying &quot;Shove: Move the target out of Close range to Short range&quot; doesn't allow for a massive dice explosion where your Might 4 tank manages eight successes and therefore sends his target 31+ meters away, and therefore to medium range, just ripe for a marksman to pick him off before he can get back to the characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","user":"Ashnak","date":".  I gave a longer explaination because I didn't read the question closely enough 07-16-2018, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","name":"Ashnak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T13:56:42-07:00","id":1235706,"title":"","content":"A doubt about Movement. Origin, p. 72 says: &quot;an unimpeded human on foot can move a number of feet each turn equal to twice their Athletics + their highest Physical Attribute.&quot;<br /> <br /> That means: &quot;(Athletics + &gt;Physical) x 2 = Feet&quot; or &quot;(2xAthletics) + &gt;Physical = Feet&quot;?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T14:05:28-07:00","id":1235708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hayashi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1235706#post1235706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A doubt about Movement. Origin, p. 72 says: &amp;quot;an unimpeded human on foot can move a number of feet each turn equal to twice their Athletics + their highest Physical Attribute.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> That means: &amp;quot;(Athletics + &gt;Physical) x 2 = Feet&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;(2xAthletics) + &gt;Physical = Feet&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially odd as Scion only seems to bother with feet in very specific circumstances","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T14:15:03-07:00","id":1235711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1235651#post1235651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe? A weakling is still going to drop the guy in Close range if he's trying for a Throw. But just saying &quot;Shove: Move the target out of Close range to Short range&quot; doesn't allow for a massive dice explosion where your Might 4 tank manages eight successes and therefore sends his target 31+ meters away, and therefore to medium range, just ripe for a marksman to pick him off before he can get back to the characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I agree completely that the system has to model big Throw/Shove outcomes, I just think it needs to model it in some other way than causing a result -&gt; meters -&gt; bands calculation, particularly since this appears to be the onyl time that meters are used for measurement, and only as an intermediate measurement to boot. Unfortunately i don't have a suggested solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/972-fairlyhyperman","name":"Fairlyhyperman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T15:26:23-07:00","id":1235731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1235708#post1235708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Especially odd as Scion only seems to bother with feet in very specific circumstances</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My doubt is purely mathematical. What should I be doubling? Only Athletics or Athletics + highest Physical?<br /> <br /> I know it's a lot specific (and probably I'll never use it), but really sounded weird when I read the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T16:09:13-07:00","id":1235741,"title":"","content":"I got one, When a character reaches Stamina 3 they gain 1 Bashing level, and another at 5, so why does the character sheet have 2 -1 and 2 -2 health levels?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T18:58:47-07:00","id":1235766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hayashi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1235731#post1235731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My doubt is purely mathematical. What should I be doubling? Only Athletics or Athletics + highest Physical?<br /> <br /> I know it's a lot specific (and probably I'll never use it), but really sounded weird when I read the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no kidding. I would personally do 2 x (Athletics + Highest Physical) if you need to","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T20:20:07-07:00","id":1235787,"title":"","content":"Any tips for fluffing Potemkin World with regards to a Tuatha Scion? My brain jumped to an idea involving a Scion of Nuada who ended up being raised in Tir na nOg after his mother's death, but upon a second read through I realized having a child raised in a place where no one ages is probably not a good idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T20:44:33-07:00","id":1235791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica1000</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1235787#post1235787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any tips for fluffing Potemkin World with regards to a Tuatha Scion? My brain jumped to an idea involving a Scion of Nuada who ended up being raised in Tir na nOg after his mother's death, but upon a second read through I realized having a child raised in a place where no one ages is probably not a good idea</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure you can. You go through a normal school and what you know its always a shame how after a while your friends end up moving, or go to a different school or something. Well that or you get people willing to use magic to update their appearance to simulate aging to prevent the kid from feeling too ostracized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T20:46:59-07:00","id":1235794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica1000</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1235787#post1235787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any tips for fluffing Potemkin World with regards to a Tuatha Scion? My brain jumped to an idea involving a Scion of Nuada who ended up being raised in Tir na nOg after his mother's death, but upon a second read through I realized having a child raised in a place where no one ages is probably not a good idea</div> </div> </div> </div>I would absolutely suggest making a S\u00edd mound for Nuada! The T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann predominately live beneath the earth inside specific hills such as how Br\u00fa na B\u00f3inne is the home of Aengus and S\u00edd Br\u00ed Leth is the home of Midir. The inside of these hills are essentially personal Terra Incognita of the figure in question, Sanctums using 1e's terminology and are large, beautiful halls that likely exit into the Otherworld beneath the surface of Ireland. As these hills functioned sort of like Royal Centers for the world beneath the ground, the immediate area surrounding the S\u00edd could be the Terra Incognita that they were raised in, likely lots of cattle, young \u00c1os S\u00edd (Sidhe) playing and being fostered. A very cool Potemkin World for the Scion to be raised in!<br /> <br /> Nuada's one is probably somewhere in Munster, as some of the mortal dynasties in the area used to use him as a legitimizing ancestor. <br /> <br /> P.S.: Your Scion's stepmothers are super cool, Macha and The Badb. They... okay, Macha probably had a bit of a hand in raising the Scion if you are looking for ideas. The Badb is just a particularly hungry bird that is good at insults.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T17:55:18-07:00","id":1238733,"title":"","content":"What Power (Knack. Purview, etc.) does Eileen uses in her tale in Scion Origin? Just curiosity question about what would be a &quot;mind reading&quot; power that subtle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T00:11:19-07:00","id":1238813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hayashi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1238733#post1238733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Power (Knack. Purview, etc.) does Eileen uses in her tale in Scion Origin? Just curiosity question about what would be a &quot;mind reading&quot; power that subtle.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had to guess? The Sage Knack &quot;Office Hours&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Offce Hours: When someone approaches you with a problem that you can solve, they gain +1 Enhancement to resolve it themselves if you work them through a solution. If you can\u2019t solve it, you gain the same bonus to all rolls to solve it on your own. These bonuses apply before rolls are made. Spend Momentum to impel a Storyguide Character to come to you with a problem in need of solving. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T13:03:24-07:00","id":1239771,"title":"","content":"Debating whether this deserves a thread or not. Basically this is to just help me with my perspective of a couple of pantheon. This is it.<br /> <br /> What are the Orisha and Manitou in the context of Divinity. Now I no that these two don't really consider themselves as Gods in the classical sense, thus I wanted to ask on what they do consider themselves as.<br /> <br /> Orisha's are consider themselves more on a monotheistic point then the others, that is they believe there is a big great God at the center of everything. This what are the Orisha then? If there not Gods then what are they and there place in Yoruban cosmology. They aren't mortals tho they have lived and ruled in actual kingdoms as kings, so they are closer to humanity then distant Gods would be, but what is their position? What are Orisha?<br /> <br /> Similar question for the Manitou, from what I gather Manitou consider themselves like spirits. That there is a spirit for everything and that is a Manitou. This what are the Manitou that we have in the Pantheon line up. What makes them different from the other smaller Manitou. Do they represent things so broad that they have such a special place? Also what qould have been there relationship with their believers? If there not Gods why would people invoke them and try to appease them. What do they represent for such a thing, are they considered to be different from the other minor manitou?<br /> <br /> Basically that's my question. Hope it ain't much, just wishing to understand it better","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T14:43:29-07:00","id":1239803,"title":"","content":"So planning on running an experiment with one of my normal group using the Origin book. Was toying with using one of the old modules for the experiment even if I'm going to have to tinker with enemy stats to make them work, but would those work or are they going to assume a higher power level than Origin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T21:01:48-07:00","id":1239889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1239803#post1239803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So planning on running an experiment with one of my normal group using the Origin book. Was toying with using one of the old modules for the experiment even if I'm going to have to tinker with enemy stats to make them work, but would those work or are they going to assume a higher power level than Origin?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd use a module as an outline, but replace any encounters with does from the Origin book.<br /> <br /> Also this is just general, but don't be afraid to start small with your encounters. Mooks leading to tougher foes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T21:21:10-07:00","id":1239894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1239889#post1239889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd use a module as an outline, but replace any encounters with does from the Origin book.<br /> <br /> Also this is just general, but don't be afraid to start small with your encounters. Mooks leading to tougher foes</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I just wanted to make sure that I wasn't operating from a false standpoint and that Hero level modules didn't assume way more power than an Origin character can field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T22:47:04-07:00","id":1239909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1239894#post1239894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, I just wanted to make sure that I wasn't operating from a false standpoint and that Hero level modules didn't assume way more power than an Origin character can field.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I imagine they kinda do, or at least other avenues. Most Origin characters can't use the Death purview to summon a Shade","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T23:49:14-07:00","id":1241711,"title":"","content":"OK, so, finally getting around to drawing up a character for a trial game using the hero rules. The creatures background seems to lack some pretty important stats missing. Looks like they're built the same as antagonists, sort of, so... how many health boxes do they generally have? Defense, initiative? Are these stats based off of dot value as well, or a flat total that only get increased by picking appropriate Qualities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T17:28:09-07:00","id":1242146,"title":"","content":"So I have a 2e question. How exactly does the book define what a primordial deity is? Like what classifies a deity as a primordial deity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T20:51:26-07:00","id":1242233,"title":"","content":"Never mind wrong sub forum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":".  Wrong Ask thread. 08-03-2018, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T20:54:08-07:00","id":1242234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1242233#post1242233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm, I'm not familiar with 2E having a classification of Primordial Deity. Can you name one of these entities or where you saw the term?<br /> <br /> As I recall it in 2e there were Least Gods, basically the gods of random knick objects like your shoes or individual grains of rice that are potentially not even sentient or sapient; Terrestrial Gods, that were lower rank and stuck in Creation; Celestial Gods, more powerful larger and more important portfolios that were generally in Yu-Shan; and the Incarnae, which was basically Sol, Luna, and the Maidens. The only thing I recall having the title of Primordial were the Primodials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm... I'm pretty certain that's <i>Exalted</i>, not Scion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T20:58:44-07:00","id":1242235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1242146#post1242146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have a 2e question. How exactly does the book define what a primordial deity is? Like what classifies a deity as a primordial deity?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Primordial is a usually vastly powerful being that almost never directly interacts with the World outside of <i>existing</i>. Nyx of the Theoi is a good example, as is the Egyptian Ogdoad. Basically, Gods look upon the World through the lens of their Callings, the human archetypes that they represent, Titans look upon the World through the lens of their Purviews, the aspects of the World that they represent, and Primordials usually don't bother to look upon the World... they just <i>are</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T21:14:55-07:00","id":1242236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1242234#post1242234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Erm... I'm pretty certain that's <i>Exalted</i>, not Scion</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, noticed when I scrolled up. The tab only says part of the thread title and I'm still getting used to actually looking at this subforum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T20:36:53-07:00","id":1244037,"title":"","content":"How could Scion be applied to a different fantastical world, like the World of Darkness, planescape, Greyhawk, Golarion, or the Forgotten Realms? It seems to me that 2e might be the better fit - I think it assumes a more active role on the part of polytheistic cults. Not sure if anyone else had this reaction, but for me Heroes sound like an amazing way to look at Aasimar especially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11630-guang","user":"guang","date":". 08-09-2018, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11630-guang","name":"guang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T09:56:28-07:00","id":1244184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1244037#post1244037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How could Scion be applied to a different fantastical world, like the World of Darkness, planescape, Greyhawk, Golarion, or the Forgotten Realms? It seems to me that 2e might be the better fit - I think it assumes a more active role on the part of polytheistic cults. Not sure if anyone else had this reaction, but for me Heroes sound like an amazing way to look at Aasimar especially.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what capacity are you talking? World of Darkness seems like the only one you couldn't just say you're a demigod and start out at high level play to emphasize that fact if all you're looking for is playing a demigod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T19:49:50-07:00","id":1244351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1244184#post1244184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what capacity are you talking? World of Darkness seems like the only one you couldn't just say you're a demigod and start out at high level play to emphasize that fact if all you're looking for is playing a demigod.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm looking more at how the differences in assumptions about interactions with the divine would shift the tone of a setting, and what else in a setting would neccesarily have to change if you incorporate the depth of mythological influence presented in Scion into another setting. How would it influence V20 Camarilla or Sabbat machinations? What about seeking Golconda? How would changing the local innkeeper from an Aasimar to a Scion affect the feel of the inn and the town? Could Strange Places and Axis Mundi add a third or fourth dimension to a dungeon crawl? How is a settlement being overrun by titanspawn different from it being overrun by goblinoids? Would the Hedge of CtL be just another Strange Place in the world? Would seeking healing at a temple after battle be a much different experience? As you can see, I'm asking more about theme, tone, and how Scion could interact (or collide) with a setting that already has it's own, entirely different, fantastical elements and assumptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11630-guang","name":"guang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T18:09:36-07:00","id":1244680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1244351#post1244351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm looking more at how the differences in assumptions about interactions with the divine would shift the tone of a setting, and what else in a setting would neccesarily have to change if you incorporate the depth of mythological influence presented in Scion into another setting. How would it influence V20 Camarilla or Sabbat machinations? What about seeking Golconda? How would changing the local innkeeper from an Aasimar to a Scion affect the feel of the inn and the town? Could Strange Places and Axis Mundi add a third or fourth dimension to a dungeon crawl? How is a settlement being overrun by titanspawn different from it being overrun by goblinoids? Would the Hedge of CtL be just another Strange Place in the world? Would seeking healing at a temple after battle be a much different experience? As you can see, I'm asking more about theme, tone, and how Scion could interact (or collide) with a setting that already has it's own, entirely different, fantastical elements and assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> (Visited) Scions are drastically more powerful in the context of their own setting, than most of the PCs you've mentioned in the context of theirs. Dropping Scions in would drastically alter said worlds. The default setting of Scion doesn't even have a &quot;Masquerade&quot; equivalent because there's no real way to logically justify why Scions and the Gods would actively keep themselves secret.<br /> <br /> There existence is inherently disruptive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-10-2018, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T06:09:56-07:00","id":1244791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1244680#post1244680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dropping Scions in would drastically alter said worlds. The default setting of Scion doesn't even have a &amp;quot;Masquerade&amp;quot; equivalent because there's no real way to logically justify why Scions and the Gods would actively keep themselves secret.<br /> <br /> There existence is inherently disruptive</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent. Why include a story element if it makes only minimal difference. So if, for example, all PCs are V20 vampires in the World of Darkness, but (non-PC) visited Scions exist in their world, what changes neccessarily must happen to the setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11630-guang","name":"guang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T06:46:41-07:00","id":1244797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1244791#post1244791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent. Why include a story element if it makes only minimal difference. So if, for example, all PCs are V20 vampires in the World of Darkness, but (non-PC) visited Scions exist in their world, what changes neccessarily must happen to the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine all the deities of death and their Scions would be really interested in how the undead presence got this much out of hand. <br /> <br /> Since you mention CtL, I imagine by World of Darkness you were conflating WoD and CofD? For the latter, people already know or suspect the supernatural is out there, somwhat like in Scion 2E. It just happens that most of it wants to eat you alive, so most people forget about it and move on. I don\u2019t think adding Scions would be much different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T12:44:28-07:00","id":1248484,"title":"","content":"Hey, I'm running my games like I do and something struck me while passing out Experience on Sunday... what, exactly, is a story Milestone. I did a doc-search and found nothing. A little help for this gnome?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T14:26:24-07:00","id":1248517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1248484#post1248484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I'm running my games like I do and something struck me while passing out Experience on Sunday... what, exactly, is a story Milestone. I did a doc-search and found nothing. A little help for this gnome?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'd say a story milestone is when the players make a decent step of progress into the story.<br /> <br /> Like If say the musical talent of people in a city are vanishing and your players discover a ritual site that's collecting the talent, that would be a milestone. The whole quest isn't over yet, you still need Why and Who and to undo it, but you found the What, and that's a step closer to solving the whole thing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T11:25:47-07:00","id":1248984,"title":"","content":"Me and my group are very confused by what we're supposed to do with contacts.<br /> <br /> The manual says:<br /> character gains two points per invocation to use to<br /> create her Contacts. She can spend these dots on either<br /> gaining additional Contacts, or making a single Contact<br /> better. Each Contact begins with one dot and one tag (see<br /> list of suggested tags below; feel free to add your own special<br /> traits depending on your needs). Each additional point<br /> placed in a single Contact adds either an additional dot or<br /> an additional tag, and these points fade at the end of the<br /> session (or whenever the contact stops being relevant in the<br /> scene, whichever comes first).<br /> <br /> So how powerful your contact is depends on how many times you've invoked it? To &quot;bring out the big guns&quot; you have to invoke a more anemic version once beforehand? That can't be right.<br /> Also, if you use a contact, the scene ends, and later you invoke it again, do they &quot;start&quot; with just one dot? And you've stressed the connection anyway?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23975-pxgentleman","name":"PXGentleman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T10:18:09-07:00","id":1249467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PXGentleman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1248984#post1248984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me and my group are very confused by what we're supposed to do with contacts.<br /> <br /> The manual says:<br /> character gains two points per invocation to use to<br /> create her Contacts. She can spend these dots on either<br /> gaining additional Contacts, or making a single Contact<br /> better. Each Contact begins with one dot and one tag (see<br /> list of suggested tags below; feel free to add your own special<br /> traits depending on your needs). Each additional point<br /> placed in a single Contact adds either an additional dot or<br /> an additional tag, and these points fade at the end of the<br /> session (or whenever the contact stops being relevant in the<br /> scene, whichever comes first).<br /> <br /> So how powerful your contact is depends on how many times you've invoked it? To &quot;bring out the big guns&quot; you have to invoke a more anemic version once beforehand? That can't be right.<br /> Also, if you use a contact, the scene ends, and later you invoke it again, do they &quot;start&quot; with just one dot? And you've stressed the connection anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were a Storyguide, I'd be okay with a PC double-tapping to cut straight to &quot;Bring the big guns&quot; for two Dots and gain the required Condition right off the bat.<br /> <br /> And if I were storyguide, the whole &quot;What if it's a new scene, does the Contact go back to one dot?&quot; would probably depend on any number of things, including what they're being called in for and how much time has passed between the scenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T08:13:04-07:00","id":1253891,"title":"","content":"Im wondering, is there a reason why both a healing preview and Healer Calling is necessary. Like what can you do that is needed to have these things be separate. Like why not have it be one Calling or Purview. Just curious to see if anyone has any thoughts on it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T16:43:27-07:00","id":1254350,"title":"","content":"Am I missing it, or is there no Riastadt power currently in War, any of the Epic Attribute Purviews, or Geas?<br /> <br /> If it ends up being a demigod level power, i\u2019m totally cool with that, just want to make sure i\u2019m not missing it (and hopefully that it shows up eventually)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T17:27:58-07:00","id":1254355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1254350#post1254350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I missing it, or is there no Riastadt power currently in War, any of the Epic Attribute Purviews, or Geas?<br /> <br /> If it ends up being a demigod level power, i\u2019m totally cool with that, just want to make sure i\u2019m not missing it (and hopefully that it shows up eventually)</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall has talked the R\u00edastrad on the Discord in passing as a potential Warrior Knack unique to Scions of the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann before, though it has not been published as of this moment. (I would also suggest that it is related somehow to a Fomorian Ancestry Origin Path of some sort due to the various motifs invoked with the various bodily features and the unique nature of it to C\u00faChulainn)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T17:51:47-07:00","id":1254358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1254355#post1254355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neall has talked the R\u00edastrad on the Discord in passing as a potential Warrior Knack unique to Scions of the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann before, though it has not been published as of this moment. (I would also suggest that it is related somehow to a Fomorian Ancestry Origin Path of some sort due to the various motifs invoked with the various bodily features and the unique nature of it to C\u00faChulainn)</div> </div> </div> </div>Given what it does, I was thinking of it letting you stack a few Boons with Visage Great and Terrible so you can unleash them together as though they\u2019re a single effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T18:31:22-07:00","id":1254373,"title":"","content":"Powers related famine and poverty would be covered by the famine and prosperity Purviews, right?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m thinking of applying the same logic as the Beast Passion and Artistry Purviews - in return to restricting effects only to the negative, the character gets a new Approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T18:59:21-07:00","id":1254380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1254358#post1254358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given what it does, I was thinking of it letting you stack a few Boons with Visage Great and Terrible so you can unleash them together as though they\u2019re a single effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't necessarily connect it to Boons in the same way that 1e did, that was mostly a failure to understand the R\u00edastrad and read everything it stated in the most literal of senses entirely devoid of any actual understanding of the meaning of the text. For instance, the fire motif that crops up in the R\u00edastrad has nothing to do with fire, it has to do with a early medieval medical theory that related Heat and Cold to Masculinity and Femininity. You can see this use of heat to represent extreme masculinity in Fergus mac Roich, as well as the the earliest form of Sir Kay we see in... The Lady of the Fountain IIRC?<br /> <br /> The only described benefits of C\u00faChulainn's R\u00edastrad is becoming physically monstrous (I will note, this doesn't bother anyone in the Sagas so I would probably not give it any Fear related features) in a very body-horror way, not a Hulking-Out sort of way. C\u00faChulainn's strength seems to be augmented in this state (see: <i>Fled Bricrenn</i>) and nothing else seems to be. It is also closely related to failure, C\u00faChulainn manifests the ability when he has failed, possibly having some sort of connection to shame which we see in other areas can cause disfigurement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T14:50:13-07:00","id":1255341,"title":"","content":"Do we have any confirmation of the pantheons that will be described in Hero? <br /> <br /> I remember reading somewhere that we'd get extras on top of the ones in Origins. Or did I imagine that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4612-solar-lantern","name":"Solar Lantern","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T15:04:54-07:00","id":1255343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar Lantern</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1255341#post1255341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have any confirmation of the pantheons that will be described in Hero? <br /> <br /> I remember reading somewhere that we'd get extras on top of the ones in Origins. Or did I imagine that?</div> </div> </div> </div>You imagined that. The 10 Pantheons given diety lists in Origins get full write ups in Hero.<br /> <br /> There are also 4 Pantheons coming in the Companion<br /> <br /> - the Yazata (Zoroastrian holy beings of Persia)<br /> - Nemetondevos (the utterly destroyed Gaulish pantheon with potential to resurrect)<br /> - Loa (the New World counterparts of the Orisha)<br /> - Atlanteans (as an example of making your own fictional pantheon)<br /> <br /> After that, the next official addition of new Pantheons will be the Demigod book. No finalized list there though the Anunna (Mesopotamian) and Bogovi (Slavic Russian) are the two safest bets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-18-2018, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T10:32:42-07:00","id":1257220,"title":"","content":"Hi guys, I'm new here. I've started a campaign in Scion: Origins with my friends and we got confused about the Paths. In the book it says every character can have how many Paths they want. but it is best if it doesn't exceed 5. In character creation we have 3: Origin, Role, Society/Pantheon.<br /> <br /> Now looking to the sample characters, they all have 4 Paths, the fourth being &quot;Pre-Visitation Scion&quot;. So we thought maybe everyone gets a fourth Path not mentioned in Character Creation if they are Scions, but after reading the book, the Pre-Visitation Scion Path is in the same category as Supernatural Paths, and when we look into the Supernatural Characters, or Denizens, the rule says these substitutes the Origin Path of the characters. Now, what is the correct way to create the Paths by the rules? Because we can just create any Path me and my players want and get the story going, but rule wise, it is a mess.<br /> <br /> Other question tied to the previous, is: A denizen can have Origin Path without being its supernatural path, and can a denizen have the Pantheon Path being his supernatrual path? Other question is: A Scion that have the Society/Pantheon Path called: Son of Loki must have another Path stating he is a Pre-Visitation Scion?<br /> <br /> Thank you for your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","user":"Oxcelot","date":". 09-25-2018, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","name":"Oxcelot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T12:20:23-07:00","id":1257231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oxcelot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1257220#post1257220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi guys, I'm new here. I've started a campaign in Scion: Origins with my friends and we got confused about the Paths. In the book it says every character can have how many Paths they want. but it is best if it doesn't exceed 5. In character creation we have 3: Origin, Role, Society/Pantheon.<br /> <br /> Now looking to the sample characters, they all have 4 Paths, the fourth being &quot;Pre-Visitation Scion&quot;. So we thought maybe everyone gets a fourth Path not mentioned in Character Creation if they are Scions, but after reading the book, the Pre-Visitation Scion Path is in the same category as Supernatural Paths, and when we look into the Supernatural Characters, or Denizens, the rule says these substitutes the Origin Path of the characters. Now, what is the correct way to create the Paths by the rules? Because we can just create any Path me and my players want and get the story going, but rule wise, it is a mess.<br /> <br /> Other question tied to the previous, is: A denizen can have Origin Path without being its supernatural path, and can a denizen have the Pantheon Path being his supernatrual path? Other question is: A Scion that have the Society/Pantheon Path called: Son of Loki must have another Path stating he is a Pre-Visitation Scion?<br /> <br /> Thank you for your time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can create any Path that makes sense for the character you want... Pre-Visitation Scion isn't a separate Path for any of the sample characters since that is already covered by their other Paths, for example, 'Hidden Blade of Agni' for Rashmi or 'Xiuhtecuhtli Reborn' for Emmanuel already means that they are Pre-Visitation Scions.It's not a separate Path unless you want it to be (Eric has 'Scion of Thos' as his Pantheon Path, for example).<br /> <br /> There is no Supernatural Path, as such... you start with an Origin Path, a Role Path and a Pantheon Path any of which can have supernatural elements, and you can tie in your Denizen nature to any of those... for example, 'Naga Prince', 'Satyr DJ' or 'Centaur pupil of Apollo' are all valid to give you access to Denizen status.<br /> <br /> And as mentioned above, no, being a Son of Loki includes being a Pre-Visitation Scion in most cases. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Hope that helped","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T13:07:17-07:00","id":1257249,"title":"","content":"Thank you Samudra, I was thinking your example would be the case, but the rules are not clearly enough. It is very similar to how aspects work in Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","name":"Oxcelot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T04:49:05-07:00","id":1259566,"title":"","content":"I am understanding correctly that the Scion Hero version currently available through backerkit is the final text for the PDF? Is the character generation fixed in that version? iirc the last time I looked into scion 2e there was an errata floating around with corrections to the character generation.<br /> <br /> Is there somewhere a version with bookmarks available?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24080-cybertier","name":"cybertier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T07:34:02-07:00","id":1259594,"title":"","content":"No that isn't the final text, there hasn't been an errata yet also Neall mentioned he's still inputting changes that was revealed in Origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T08:05:32-07:00","id":1259598,"title":"","content":"Oh, has there been any ETA on the final text? The Kickstarter and backerkit all claim it's already finalized and in layout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24080-cybertier","name":"cybertier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T08:23:28-07:00","id":1259600,"title":"","content":"Its in layout yes, when thats done every backer will received a pdf for it and the errata will start, after the errata is collected, they will input the changes then they will released the book with its final text. As of now we are just waiting to get the layout pdfs so we can see what needs to be changed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-17T18:51:16-07:00","id":1261216,"title":"","content":"I just had a conversation with the great <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a> And he told me a friend of his told him the mayan gods don't have any positive view of death,i did some googling after that and i saw the mayas seem to think death and the underworld are 100% evil.So i was wondering,woud it make sense from a game design point to leave the k'uh underworld on the Titans hands, perhaps even making the underworld ,Xibalba, A primordial of Death that is insanely evil? As a place people are desperate not to go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-17T20:35:27-07:00","id":1261230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1261216#post1261216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just had a conversation with the great <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> And he told me a friend of his told him the mayan gods don't have any positive view of death,i did some googling after that and i saw the mayas seem to think death and the underworld are 100% evil.So i was wondering,woud it make sense from a game design point to leave the k'uh underworld on the Titans hands, perhaps even making the underworld ,Xibalba, A primordial of Death that is insanely evil? As a place people are desperate not to go?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not seeing why that would be necessary. There are plenty of evil gods. I mean it could be in Titan hands, but just being evil doesn\u2019t seem to me like an inherent reason for that to be the case. Is it in an adversarial role to the rest of the gods?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-17T20:44:23-07:00","id":1261233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1261230#post1261230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m not seeing why that would be necessary. There are plenty of evil gods. I mean it could be in Titan hands, but just being evil doesn\u2019t seem to me like an inherent reason for that to be the case. Is it in an adversarial role to the rest of the gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Xibalban Lords killed the Hero twins uncle and father and were terribly cruel and seemed to have nothing human in them. The story of their battle against the twins and defeat is the most famous story of the Maya and K'iche people<br /> So yeah,they had an adversarial role","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T09:26:36-07:00","id":1262165,"title":"","content":"When a God Incarnates into a Scion he is not in the Overworld, correct? One of my player is toying with the idea of an Incarnate of Kali and I'm not sure if that would mean the Dark Mother would leave the Titanomachy while Incarnating or if she would be metaphysically in two planes at the same time.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T09:30:01-07:00","id":1262167,"title":"","content":"From what I'm aware they exist at both places simultaneously, in fact from what the text implies the gods can maintain multiple incarnations all over the place","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T09:51:30-07:00","id":1262176,"title":"","content":"Unless one of the pieces of her mantle for what ever reason (self inflicted, or the plot of a powerful rival god or Titan) was broken away and Incarnated into a whole separate aspect in the world as the character. In which case the 'real' Kali wouldn't have access to that particular aspect any more as it's alive somewhere else as its own thing.<br /> <br /> Make for a Hell of a meeting one day, and the character and Kali possibly becoming a dual-natured-deity a la the Morrigan or Brigid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T13:45:23-07:00","id":1262215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1262165#post1262165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a God Incarnates into a Scion he is not in the Overworld, correct? One of my player is toying with the idea of an Incarnate of Kali and I'm not sure if that would mean the Dark Mother would leave the Titanomachy while Incarnating or if she would be metaphysically in two planes at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The basic Incarnate Origin requires that your Deity Self (or at least that Mantle) be dead yes... that being said, Hindu Myth is chock full of Heroic Incarnations that are absolutely Player Character material, and whose over-selves absolutely exist simultaneously in their own realms (or whichever realm they want to be in frankly), so in this case the Incarnate Origin doesn't work as written for your character idea or Hindu Myth in general.<br /> <br /> <i>That being said</i>, the Yoga Purview exists, and it is absolutely fitting and in line with myth to say that Yoga lets the Deva create Incarnate Scions without needing to die (since Yoga is literally what lets them create Avatars in the first place in myth). So no, Kali doesn't need to be dead for your character to be an Incarnate of her. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, kudos on the character idea, I hope it ends up happening... Kali is a pretty amazing Goddess, if I do say so myself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T00:17:16-07:00","id":1262482,"title":"","content":"Ok, I don't have just ONE question, but some. But let's go...<br /> <br /> 1. How the system deals with shields (ancient or modern)? Are they simply armor tags? <br /> <br /> 2. I was thinking about a Scion of Chang'e that has as one of her Birthrights a rabbit, that is inteligent (as a normal mortal human), able to speak (just not very prone to that), and, as his cousins that are still on the moon with Chang'e, he is a &quot;magic potion brewer&quot;. No, he can not make the Immortality Elixir, 'cause he is not wise/powerfull enough (yet). But mostly he can make some lesser boosters (+1e) like lesser healing potions and stuffs as that when previously asked. Would that be a Creature or is it more to a Follower? Maybe even a Relic itself (except for the fact he is alive), that ables the Scion to produce these items previously mentioned (Creator Calling, maybe?). So... I got really stuck on that one. What really grinds my gears is that: He is inteligent and speaks. So he is not a &quot;Creature&quot;. But I really can not immagine he being useful in combat, so he is not a Follower... And he is alive, so probably not a Relic...<br /> <br /> 2.5 I thought (just now) in make him a Guide, with a Guide Stunt that allows the Scion to create these potions/single use alchemical items (it must be hard to brew things without opposing thumbs) with Crafting tests. Is this... OK? A single character can have more than one Guide? (In this specific case, the Scion already has one)<br /> <br /> 3. When choosing the &quot;Any&quot; Knacks (Scent the Divine, Somebody Watches Me, etc.), I must yet pick one Calling, that will not get a Knack yet? That Knack goes to the &quot;Any&quot; 'Calling'. But later I can get another point in this first Calling and get a second (or first, I think more actually) Knack in this Calling? Or this is all wrong and the way to do this is not have this &quot;to be turned into an General Knack&quot; Calling and get the General Knack directly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T04:23:11-07:00","id":1262493,"title":"","content":"Yeah I would give the rabbit as a Guide, makes most sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T10:44:37-07:00","id":1262552,"title":"","content":"Probably really obvious, but you don\u2019t need to perform a Motif to use a Boon, right? Just a Marvel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T11:45:12-07:00","id":1262560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1262552#post1262552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably really obvious, but you don\u2019t need to perform a Motif to use a Boon, right? Just a Marvel?</div> </div> </div> </div>You do not require a Motif to use a Boon, only a Marvel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T03:22:48-07:00","id":1262641,"title":"","content":"Are the Japanese EVER going to get a deity who has the fire purview? Or do they just assume Japan never discovered fire until the mid-19th Century? I have noticed a rather disturbing lack of one so far in 2e and most decidedly in 1e. Hence why I ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T03:43:57-07:00","id":1262644,"title":"","content":"Well that depends. Do you know any prominent kami of Fire? They aren't making up Gods willy nilly, they are using actual Kami's for the writeups which are worshiped in Shintoism. And sometimes those deities just aren't seen as representing certain stuff, you can't just have a fire god just because you think their needs to be a fire, not everything is really the convenient. Now to answer my own question on whether I know of a prominent Fire kami, I do actually but he's more of a Titan then God so not nice","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T04:23:20-07:00","id":1262650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1262641#post1262641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Are the Japanese EVER going to get a deity who has the fire purview? Or do they just assume Japan never discovered fire until the mid-19th Century? I have noticed a rather disturbing lack of one so far in 2e and most decidedly in 1e. Hence why I ask.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are Eight Million Kami and only so many Gods you can write up in a book... If you want to see a Fire using Kami and know of one, you are free to write then up yourself... And please stop with the 'Japan knew Fire existed' line, it's getting ridiculous. The authors are not, on any way shape or form, implying that the Japanese did not know that Fire existed just because they didn't put ina God of Fire... That line of argument makes zero sense and also makes it very difficult to take the rest of your post with any degree of seriousness.<br /> <br /> The Hindus knew how to smith things... They don't have a Forge God on the roster either, and it would be equally mindless to shout that the writers are implying that Hindu civilization didn't know how to make stuff. The Greeks were also perfectly aware that forests exist... They don't need to have a Wild God written up, just as the Aztecs were perfectly aware that the Moon existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T04:45:31-07:00","id":1262656,"title":"","content":"Fire is a thing that appears in Japanese myth but it\u2019s never really a major force mythologically speaking. It\u2019s a tool but not really a character. <br /> <br /> It may just be that something they see as such a common tool of mortals isn\u2019t divine. While living here I\u2019ve heard and seen lots of stories related to water, wind, earth, and animals talking to people, but Fire isn\u2019t something I\u2019ve seen associated with characters.<br /> <br /> Not every culture considers everything to have the same significance. Fire as the driving force of civilization is something I\u2019ve more and more seen as a Greek focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","user":"Thrythlind","date":". 10-25-2018, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T06:12:39-07:00","id":1262665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1262641#post1262641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Are the Japanese EVER going to get a deity who has the fire purview? Or do they just assume Japan never discovered fire until the mid-19th Century? I have noticed a rather disturbing lack of one so far in 2e and most decidedly in 1e. Hence why I ask.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many Pantheons lack certain concepts, not because their culture did not realize that concept existed, but because that concept held less importance to them in a divine sense. There are, of course, Kami who would be associated with Fire as there are a nearly countless number of Kami ranging from major modern figures to all but forgotten regional early medieval figures. However, none of these were chosen to be in Hero for design and research purposes.<br /> <br /> I believe it is appallingly inappropriate of you to accuse the authors of assuming Japan not having access to fire until the mid-19th century, and something that falls apart with even the minimal level of critical thinking. Susano-O has Forge for his arrival from Korea narratives where he introduced metallurgy to Japan, and his sword-smithing shrine in Izumo. The Kami are depicted carrying various metal objects in their ancient artwork. Therefore, the authors were in fact aware that Japan has had access to fire for thousands of years. They chose not to give anyone Fire as the figures presented in Hero are a snapshot of the most important, and most interesting. Future expansions to the Pantheon might add a Fire figure to the Pantheon, but it has nothing to do with your suggestion that Japan did not discover fire. By that same logic the Irish never noticed the sun existed which is clearly preposterous.<br /> <br /> I believe the last time you inquired about this someone wrote up Hi-no-Kagutsuchi as a Divine Parent for you to show an example of a Kami with Fire who is not written up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T08:46:15-07:00","id":1262683,"title":"","content":"My question is more fluff-related than crunch, but I feel like the errata thread is too strict for this sort thing, so I'll ask it here. Why aren't Izanagi and Izanami mentioned in the cosmology subsection of the Kami chapter? I understand that some pantheons might not have much in the way of primordials worth talking about, but considering that they were parental options in 1e, I have a hard time believing the Kami would be one of them. There's got to be more lore than just the name drop in Amaterasu and Susano-o's sections! I can only imagine the omission of what would probably be a whole paragraph must be a deliberate creative choice, but it seems more like an oversight to me...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12598-karasu-sama","name":"Karasu-sama","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T09:39:25-07:00","id":1262687,"title":"","content":"I'd say word limit but really I don't know. I agree with you that them not being there doesn't make much sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 10-25-2018, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T10:10:42-07:00","id":1262690,"title":"","content":"Maybe its one of those things like they hard in the Origins book where they deliberately left out a few major players in pantheons as a reminder that the book isn't meant to be the complete list and encourage people to make their own if they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T10:59:22-07:00","id":1262694,"title":"","content":"Can anyone offer a summation of how the Virtue Track is intended to work? I had hoped that the Hero pdf would have clarified things from Origin, but I\u2019m still somewhat in dark. I\u2019m fine with the track itself and how the Virtuous condition is triggered when the needle pegs to one side or the other.<br /> <br /> The main question that I have is what types of actions move the needle along the track; sure, actions related to one of the two virtues, but any particular type of action?<br /> <br /> For example, a Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann with Honor and Prowess virtues. What does it take to shift the needle towards Honor? Any honorable action? One that involves a dice roll? An honorable die action that scores a lot of successes? One that involves a Momentum expenditure? Legend expenditure? Feat of Scale? My feeling is that there should be some kind of objective measure, because Honor or Prowess are fairly easy things to accomplish, roleplaying-wise, and accepting that any honorable or mighty act moves the needle would result in hitting the Virtuous condition all the time.<br /> <br /> Was there something in the Origin or Hero books to address this that I missed?<br /> <br /> Plus, the Yoga innate power, says \u201cyou may allow another player to spend Momentum on an action without having to draw on one of their Virtues\u201d. Did the rules for Momentum expenditure change, or is this an error?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/972-fairlyhyperman","name":"Fairlyhyperman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T11:16:26-07:00","id":1262695,"title":"","content":"So the description of how Virtues work and the Virtuous Condition seem to have repeated text. My gut says that you are probably able to spend Momentum normally, but get a small benefit when doing so aligns with a Virtue (probably like +1 die or something). And if you have the Virtuous Condition (or the Yoga innate power), you get a large bonus (twice as many dice as Momentum spent). <br /> <br /> However, that is just a gut feeling - I could be wildly off-base.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T15:06:39-07:00","id":1262745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1262641#post1262641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Are the Japanese EVER going to get a deity who has the fire purview? Or do they just assume Japan never discovered fire until the mid-19th Century? I have noticed a rather disturbing lack of one so far in 2e and most decidedly in 1e. Hence why I ask.</div> </div> </div> </div>The most significant Kami of Fire (Kagu-tschui) is pretty importantly dead and not a subject of significant honor to my knowledge in Shintoism compared with the big name Pantheon members. That said, he could make a good candidate to play an Incarnate Scion of.<br /> <br /> The other possibility for a major Kami with the fire purview would be Konohanasakuya, as goddesses volcanoes (along with Mount Fuji specifically, and cherry blossoms). She\u2019s up there with Tenjin as a strong bet for the Kami\u2019s new god in the Companion.<br /> <br /> They didn\u2019t choose to exclude the fire purview for any sort of statement. They\u2019re just trying to accurately reflect each of the given major gods of each pantheon. Some concepts are more prominent in some mythic traditions than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-25-2018, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-26T02:47:17-07:00","id":1262815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1262695#post1262695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the description of how Virtues work and the Virtuous Condition seem to have repeated text. My gut says that you are probably able to spend Momentum normally, but get a small benefit when doing so aligns with a Virtue (probably like +1 die or something). And if you have the Virtuous Condition (or the Yoga innate power), you get a large bonus (twice as many dice as Momentum spent).<br /> <br /> However, that is just a gut feeling - I could be wildly off-base.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly I think some where in the mythos he was brought back to life. As he holds the position of deity of the forge. Also there is one other deity who can hold the position. He's regarded as the God of Fire, Hearth and Cooking. His name isKojin. He is the opposite of Kagu-tsuchi. Where as Kagu is what happens when fire is used destructively. He is what happens when fire is harnessed and turned towards good. I just think it's a bit shameful they can't(won't) do it since there are plenty of examples of such deities in the mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-26T05:20:32-07:00","id":1262826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1262815#post1262815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interestingly I think some where in the mythos he was brought back to life. As he holds the position of deity of the forge. Also there is one other deity who can hold the position. He's regarded as the God of Fire, Hearth and Cooking. His name isKojin. He is the opposite of Kagu-tsuchi. Where as Kagu is what happens when fire is used destructively. He is what happens when fire is harnessed and turned towards good. I just think it's a bit shameful they can't(won't) do it since there are plenty of examples of such deities in the mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s neither \u201ccan\u2019t\u201d nor \u201cwon\u2019t\u201d. It\u2019s they made a list of FIFTEEN of the most significant of the major kami (tying for first place between the Pantheons for most included deities in the corebook!) and none of them happened to have the fire purview. No choice was made to exclude it. It just didn\u2019t happen to come up with the fifteen gods that they chose to go in. The list isn\u2019t intended to be exhaustive, as the text discusses how easy it is to play the Scion of an unlisted god - you just need to pick one appropriate purview (so Fire) to be inherent, and one of your three Callings needs to conceivably come from them (so I\u2019m guessing Creator or Guardian for a Scion of Kojin).<br /> <br /> Edit: Reading up on K\u014djin, Judge would be the third viable Calling choice.<br /> <br /> Thanks for pointing him out! Adding him as a viable patron deity for my own table!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-26-2018, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T10:03:37-07:00","id":1264289,"title":"","content":"Question : You can buy extra Knacks, but you can only use a number of Knack equal to your Calling dots. But how do you manage which Knacks are &quot;used&quot; and which are not?<br /> <br /> Does the player need to &quot;equip&quot; a set of Knacks at the start of the session and is stuck with this choice until the next session? How often do you let your players swap out their set of Knacks? Is there a cost associated?<br /> <br /> Maybe I missed this information. If it's not specified, how do you manage this in your game?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3816-emperorclydeiv","name":"EmperorClydeIV","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T13:05:41-07:00","id":1264318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EmperorClydeIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1264289#post1264289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question : You can buy extra Knacks, but you can only use a number of Knack equal to your Calling dots. But how do you manage which Knacks are &quot;used&quot; and which are not?<br /> <br /> Does the player need to &quot;equip&quot; a set of Knacks at the start of the session and is stuck with this choice until the next session? How often do you let your players swap out their set of Knacks? Is there a cost associated?<br /> <br /> Maybe I missed this information. If it's not specified, how do you manage this in your game?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The way we have been playing it is to handle that as a part of the 'tweaking' that can be done between play sessions. I believe Scion: Origins refers to being able to swap in a new Knack that you have purchased so we assumed that would apply for picking which Knacks are available for your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T01:41:51-07:00","id":1264392,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you can swap your knacks between sessions.<br /> <br /> A few GMs don't like making their players thinking they should know perfectly what they'll need, so many of them set it up so that you basically have blank slots and can assign them when you need it, but once you do that they're set for the rest of the session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-04T20:45:31-08:00","id":1264683,"title":"","content":"Do you get the Innate Power for any purview you have access to, whether innate or channeled through a relic or guide, or only from innate Purviews?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23991-bacchicone","name":"BacchicOne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-04T20:53:13-08:00","id":1264684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BacchicOne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1264683#post1264683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you get the Innate Power for any purview you have access to, whether innate or channeled through a relic or guide, or only from innate Purviews?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any Purview you have access to. If you can perform a Marvel from it, you have the innate power (so always if the Purview is inherent, but you can lose it if it\u2019s tied a Relic you lose possession of, or if you fall out with your Guide).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-14-2018, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T19:35:14-08:00","id":1267485,"title":"","content":"Can anyone clarify &quot;Not a Fighter&quot; the heroic lover knack? What defines a partner - is any party member a partner? and what does the additionally refer to...all of it, or just the second part?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24323-zipdrive","name":"ZipDrive","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T18:44:05-08:00","id":1267761,"title":"","content":"A doubt about Knacks and numbers in Character Creation.<br /> <br /> The book says: &quot;Choose three Callings (p. XX). At least one of your<br /> character\u2019s Callings must come from their divine patron\u2019s<br /> three Favored Callings.<br /> Your character receives two dots in one of their<br /> Callings and one dot each in the other two.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ok. That makes think in:<br /> Calling 1 **<br /> Calling 2 *<br /> Calling 3 *<br /> <br /> Later, in the Finishing Steps Stage, it says: &quot;[...] and either two additional Knacks or four points of Birthrights at this point in character creation.&quot;<br /> <br /> I tried to suppose that these additional Knacks would mean additional Calling points too, but most of the Ready Characters are more like:<br /> Calling 1 ***<br /> Calling 2 *<br /> Calling 3 *<br /> <br /> Where is this aditional point in Calling 1 coming from?<br /> <br /> Another thing: I'm really missing something or most of the Ready Characters are missing some points in Birthrights. Most of them I see as having 6 or even 5 points in BRs.<br /> <br /> Another thing (2): What means the &quot;Pantheon Permission&quot; in the Ready Made Characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23841,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","user":"Hayashi","date":". 11-16-2018, 05:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T18:51:13-08:00","id":1267762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZipDrive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1267485#post1267485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone clarify &quot;Not a Fighter&quot; the heroic lover knack? What defines a partner - is any party member a partner? and what does the additionally refer to...all of it, or just the second part?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I suppose that &quot;partner&quot; in this means &quot;ally&quot;, another member of the Band, etc. The text also uses &quot;this effect&quot;, so I think it refers to the disengage bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T06:01:58-08:00","id":1267815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hayashi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1267761#post1267761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A doubt about Knacks and numbers in Character Creation.<br /> <br /> The book says: &quot;Choose three Callings (p. XX). At least one of your<br /> character\u2019s Callings must come from their divine patron\u2019s<br /> three Favored Callings.<br /> Your character receives two dots in one of their<br /> Callings and one dot each in the other two.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ok. That makes think in:<br /> Calling 1 **<br /> Calling 2 *<br /> Calling 3 *<br /> <br /> Later, in the Finishing Steps Stage, it says: &quot;[...] and either two additional Knacks or four points of Birthrights at this point in character creation.&quot;<br /> <br /> I tried to suppose that these additional Knacks would mean additional Calling points too, but most of the Ready Characters are more like:<br /> Calling 1 ***<br /> Calling 2 *<br /> Calling 3 *<br /> <br /> Where is this aditional point in Calling 1 coming from?<br /> <br /> Another thing: I'm really missing something or most of the Ready Characters are missing some points in Birthrights. Most of them I see as having 6 or even 5 points in BRs.<br /> <br /> Another thing (2): What means the &quot;Pantheon Permission&quot; in the Ready Made Characters?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1.) I believe that the extra Calling point comes from character creation in Origin. It just isn't spelled out really well.<br /> <br /> 2.) Check the errata thread. It is closed but someone may have reported this already.<br /> <br /> 3.) Not sure where you are seeing this. Can you point to a page reference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T15:24:28-08:00","id":1268059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saedar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1267815#post1267815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1.) I believe that the extra Calling point comes from character creation in Origin. It just isn't spelled out really well.<br /> <br /> 2.) Check the errata thread. It is closed but someone may have reported this already.<br /> <br /> 3.) Not sure where you are seeing this. Can you point to a page reference?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 3.) The Ready-Made Character Sheets themselves. So, p. 173, 175, 177, 179.<br /> <br /> All of them have &quot;Pantheon permission&quot;s in their &quot;Effects&quot; session. <br /> <br /> 4.) (?) What happens when a Tuatha breaks a geis? He/She just... Gets another?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T00:49:42-08:00","id":1268199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hayashi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1268059#post1268059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4.) (?) What happens when a Tuatha breaks a geis? He/She just... Gets another?</div> </div> </div> </div>After they lose all their Legend Points, yes. <br /> <br /> And just gonna once again <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1etYiuHfHR-nTI5obsKhL44stbRmLkuvw2Z6qae_lbWM/edit\" target=\"_blank\">relink</a> this FAQ I put together a bit ago","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T11:52:46-08:00","id":1268935,"title":"","content":"If I want to create an Origin character having a Wizard concept (something like Harry Dresden from Dresden Files) that can do minor tricks, could I get the Birthrights options in character creation to have some relics with Purviews, and use Boons from these Purviews working Marvels like the Denizens do in Scion Hero?<br /> <br /> If not, can the Bitrhrights have some kind of &quot;power&quot; that emulates a Boon without needing Legend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","user":"Oxcelot","date":". 11-19-2018, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","name":"Oxcelot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T13:23:49-08:00","id":1268956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oxcelot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1268935#post1268935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I want to create an Origin character having a Wizard concept (something like Harry Dresden from Dresden Files) that can do minor tricks, could I get the Birthrights options in character creation to have some relics with Purviews, and use Boons from these Purviews working Marvels like the Denizens do in Scion Hero?<br /> <br /> If not, can the Bitrhrights have some kind of &quot;power&quot; that emulates a Boon without needing Legend?</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW Harry\u2019s probably at Hero level power wise.<br /> <br /> None of what you\u2019re asking for is currently in the rules (they may be later when Sorcerers get their own supplement)*, but obviously ask your GM!<br /> <br /> * From Neall\u2019s comments on the Discord it seems that there were planned to be more info on Sorcerers, but the concept developed to the point where they have such viability as PCs that they need more in-depth stand alone rules. In theory they\u2019ll span the power spectrum from mortal occultists at Origins level all the way up to Baba Yaga at God level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-19-2018, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T10:05:35-08:00","id":1269855,"title":"","content":"I'm very confused by the tension pool - is there a maximum? I've read somewhere (can't remember) no...but Traitor's resolution says fill the Tension pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24323-zipdrive","name":"ZipDrive","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T22:02:10-08:00","id":1270279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1268956#post1268956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> RAW Harry\u2019s probably at Hero level power wise.<br /> <br /> None of what you\u2019re asking for is currently in the rules (they may be later when Sorcerers get their own supplement)*, but obviously ask your GM!<br /> <br /> * From Neall\u2019s comments on the Discord it seems that there were planned to be more info on Sorcerers, but the concept developed to the point where they have such viability as PCs that they need more in-depth stand alone rules. In theory they\u2019ll span the power spectrum from mortal occultists at Origins level all the way up to Baba Yaga at God level.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you. I'm <i>Storyguiding</i> a newly campaign of Scion Origin, and we didn't fleshed too much the world, but we're taking heavy inspirations from Dresden Files because in our campaign the Supernatural World doesn't have the mask, but it is not much present. It will become more present because of the player characters awakening. After the first &quot;quest&quot; I'll let the players change things in their characters if they feel it would be better, and one of these characters is a Priestess of the Moon, daughter of Tsukyomi. We were thinking about making some kind of sorcery or similar because of the character background.<br /> <br /> I was thinking, and maybe we could use relics for marvels, but instead of paying legend, the Storyguide could get Tension everytime an Origin character tries to &quot;do magic&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","name":"Oxcelot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T09:01:32-08:00","id":1270612,"title":"","content":"Hi all, had our first 2nd: Origins yesterday and for the most of it I really like how the new system works as a whole (we made several mistakes of course but all in all it was pretty refreshing). I know everything now is more about storyguiding/telling than about actual combat but I had several questions about some of the stunts/effects:<br /> <br /> 1. Within the first few fights I've found that every single one of my mooks (most of them having 2 healths because of Group tactic) were just being poked (as per the 0s ''inflict damage'') and tripped to the ground (as per the 1s ''trip). They would then try to rise up from prone and most likely instantly taken out by trying to do so (as per the ''rising up from prone'' rule). My question is: is it too easy to just put everyone to the ground for 1 mere success, or did I build my encounter wrong? <br /> <br /> 2. Can a pinned target (as per the ranged attack 'pin'' (variable success) stunt) use pin against someone else or does he need to resolve his condition first to apply any?<br /> <br /> 3. Some poisons or flairs (like Dread gaze) can cause the ''paralyzed'' status. Does a paralyzed target still benefits from his natural 1 defense or is he considered helpless?<br /> <br /> Thank you for you time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4754-ironskin","name":"Ironskin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T18:55:40-08:00","id":1270733,"title":"","content":"pls, delete this post. The following has made already including quotes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23841,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","user":"Hayashi","date":". 11-25-2018, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T18:56:32-08:00","id":1270734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironskin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1270612#post1270612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi all, had our first 2nd: Origins yesterday and for the most of it I really like how the new system works as a whole (we made several mistakes of course but all in all it was pretty refreshing). I know everything now is more about storyguiding/telling than about actual combat but I had several questions about some of the stunts/effects:<br /> <br /> 1. Within the first few fights I've found that every single one of my mooks (most of them having 2 healths because of Group tactic) were just being poked (as per the 0s ''inflict damage'') and tripped to the ground (as per the 1s ''trip). They would then try to rise up from prone and most likely instantly taken out by trying to do so (as per the ''rising up from prone'' rule). My question is: is it too easy to just put everyone to the ground for 1 mere success, or did I build my encounter wrong?<br /> <br /> 2. Can a pinned target (as per the ranged attack 'pin'' (variable success) stunt) use pin against someone else or does he need to resolve his condition first to apply any?<br /> <br /> 3. Some poisons or flairs (like Dread gaze) can cause the ''paralyzed'' status. Does a paralyzed target still benefits from his natural 1 defense or is he considered helpless?<br /> <br /> Thank you for you time</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a great wise as the rest of this forum myself, but lets see how can I help.<br /> <br /> 1. p. 118 has the modifiers to &quot;being prone/laying on the ground&quot;. Basically, you get more defense against ranged attacks (what is good), but get in trouble if you have someone at melee (and that's bad. Supposing the mook has just being tripped, I think that's really bad for him).<br /> <br /> 2. For being pinned, the target must first suffer a grapple. To pin someone, you must to be in control of the grapple, so I think not. The target would have to first have to recover from the pin (v. 1), start a grapple against someone and then pin the other guy.<br /> <br /> 3. Also got me confused. I would say that a paralyzed target has Defense 0, but that would not make a HUGE difference. OR, I would say that he has Defense 1, but can not make Defense Stunts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T16:52:42-08:00","id":1271872,"title":"","content":"If one is making a character somewhat in the mold of a classic West European style wizard, could Forge be used as a spellbook instead of, well, and actual forge or alchemical lab? Also, if one were interested in a fantasy-world campaign, which of the Pantheon-specifc Purviews would work best for Western European/D&amp;D-style magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T17:28:47-08:00","id":1271879,"title":"","content":"Most iconic D&amp;D spells would be done via other Purviews rather than a PSP, but Heku I think along with the Netjer Pantheon Motif is going to come the closest to western high ritual magic. I can think of a lot of Marvels you could do with someone\u2019s true name, summonings, banishments, etc.<br /> <br /> That said, Metamorphosis has the obvious potential of bringing sorcery common in Western fairy tales to bare (in large part because a lot of those fairy tales are influenced by Greco-Roman myth, Ovid\u2019s Metamorphosis in particular!)<br /> <br /> <br /> A spell book Relic would be a good way to add your own Motif for alchemy and ritual spellcraft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T10:07:56-08:00","id":1276475,"title":"","content":"It might have been answered before, but I couldnt find anything, so I am gonna ask directly: if you have a Relic that gives you access to a Purview, but no Boon on that purview, do you still get the Innate Powers of that Purview?<br /> <br /> Thank you everyone for your attention and answers, have a Merry Christmas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T10:14:53-08:00","id":1276479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1276475#post1276475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might have been answered before, but I couldnt find anything, so I am gonna ask directly: if you have a Relic that gives you access to a Purview, but no Boon on that purview, do you still get the Innate Powers of that Purview?<br /> <br /> Thank you everyone for your attention and answers, have a Merry Christmas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed you do have access to the innate regardless of if you have the boon or not. Not only with purview accessed with relics but with purview from guides as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T14:25:37-08:00","id":1276526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1276479#post1276479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed you do have access to the innate regardless of if you have the boon or not. Not only with purview accessed with relics but with purview from guides as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you\u2019re capable of doing Marvels with a given purview (whether it\u2019s your inherent Purview, you possess a Relic, or are favored by a Guide), you have the Innate automatically, Boons or not.<br /> <br /> That of course means if you lose the Relic or have a falling out with your Guide you lose the associated Innates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T15:58:03-08:00","id":1276533,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the answer, it greatly helps.<br /> <br /> Also, as I am asking, I just noticed that all the characters in the book have 2 boons, besides having only legend one. Do you know why?<br /> <br /> // I found the answer of my own question. For some reason, I never read the Boons description on the character creation, just the legend levels that say that legend one has one boon.<br /> Thank you everybody anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12934,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","user":"Manbat","date":". 12-24-2018, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T03:33:04-08:00","id":1276772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1276533#post1276533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the answer, it greatly helps.<br /> <br /> Also, as I am asking, I just noticed that all the characters in the book have 2 boons, besides having only legend one. Do you know why?<br /> <br /> // I found the answer of my own question. For some reason, I never read the Boons description on the character creation, just the legend levels that say that legend one has one boon.<br /> Thank you everybody anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that should get caught in the last round of errata. The number of Boons should be Legend + 1","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T18:08:32-08:00","id":1285447,"title":"","content":"I'm reviving this discussion with a question: Do you guys have ideas about what Titans or titanspawn could be related to vampires? I'm thinking in making a vampire cult that wants to free a titan or titanspawn. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","name":"Oxcelot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T18:27:11-08:00","id":1285450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oxcelot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1285447#post1285447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reviving this discussion with a question: Do you guys have ideas about what Titans or titanspawn could be related to vampires? I'm thinking in making a vampire cult that wants to free a titan or titanspawn. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Etruscan/Roman Titan Manae (Death) springs to mind.<br /> <br /> Mayans have hostile death titans associated with underworld bat demons with night and blood sacrifice associations that would conflate nicely. Hun-Came and Vucub-Came would be the Ki\u2019che version as Lords of Xibalba where you also get Camazotz and his ilk. Ah Puch for the Yucatec version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T01:51:29-08:00","id":1288209,"title":"","content":"It is not mentioned that Poseidon had a wife, but he did have a wife known as Libya which bore him several sons. Why is this not mentioned and how can I incorporate them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T02:07:53-08:00","id":1288210,"title":"","content":"Libya, if I am not wrong is a mortal/scion, granddaughter of Zeus (like half of the kings in myths). Probably Poseidon turned her into Demigod so she could live with him in the bottom of the see, and they had 2 sons that are somehow important as their grand(...)grandsons are Perseus and Dionizus. Otherwise, there is not much about Libya.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T13:21:30-08:00","id":1288378,"title":"","content":"Okay, I looked into it more, and maybe they are saving it for the Imazighen mythology, as there are records or contact between them and Greeks in history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T19:58:03-08:00","id":1290976,"title":"","content":"Okay, so Origins mentions there are supernatural consequences for failing a deed at Hero and beyond, but I can't seem to find what those might be; Failure Deeds seem to kind of count, but those seem like those are deliberately pursued rather than failing *at* a Deed. Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T