lue":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T03:57:49-07:00","id":1494780,"title":"","content":"Ok, question for second edition, saints and monsters.<br /> Why are some sorcerer techniques described under it's working (p. 66-75) and another has a whole section for techniques (p. 75-78). What is a diffence between these two types of techniques?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25570-ilicius","name":"Ilicius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T04:58:17-07:00","id":1495418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ilicius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1494780#post1494780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, question for second edition, saints and monsters.<br /> Why are some sorcerer techniques described under it's working (p. 66-75) and another has a whole section for techniques (p. 75-78). What is a diffence between these two types of techniques?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is none as far as i know.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26520-mugbearer23","name":"Mugbearer23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T07:49:40-08:00","id":1496695,"title":"","content":"I was reading the new manuscript for God and I have a question. Hero and Demigod can regain spend Legend by sacrificing to their parents or pantheon or by Fatebinding. In God, the only method metioned is resolving prayers. But do you still gain Legend by Sacrifice and how it is expended (do they need to dedicace their sacrifice to something)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26068-apregis","name":"Apregis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26068_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T02:22:05-08:00","id":1497079,"title":"","content":"Does Scion: Dragon describe the dragons/heirs' attitude to various pantheons and their scions? Does the book specifically mention the Aesir, Netjer and Theoi? If it does, could someone post the sentence of paragraph mentioning those pantheons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8145-voidmaster","name":"VoidMaster","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T17:35:39-07:00","id":1505393,"title":"","content":"The Invoke for the Lodestone Fatebound Realm (Demigod p.140) cuts off halfway though a sentence. What does Invoking a Lodestone Realm do for you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-15T10:07:46-07:00","id":1505441,"title":"","content":"Can a Divine Scion take a Titanic calling if their divine parent doesn't have one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T06:37:14-07:00","id":1505486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1505441#post1505441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Divine Scion take a Titanic calling if their divine parent doesn't have one?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not. I don't recall any rule against it and there are deities with those paths; while it's possible albeit difficult and even more dangerous for Titanic Scions to ascend to godhood, at no point in the discussion does &quot;and this is the way Gods with Titanic Callings enter the picture. <br /> <br /> I want to say Titanomachy is even explicit in its permissions for a Divine PC to have these callings but I'm at work right now. It might create a strained relationship with your parent but it's not like that's unrelated territory to most myth bases or the human experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T07:53:40-07:00","id":1505541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1505486#post1505486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to say Titanomachy is even explicit in its permissions for a Divine PC to have these callings but I'm at work right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got you covered:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Titanomachy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The following Knacks are available for characters that have one or more of the Titan Callings: Adversary, Destroyer, Monster, Primeval, or Tyrant.<br /> Many of these Knacks may seem appropriate for Scions of Gods that aren\u2019t particularly Titanic; and some Gods may fit the definition of one of the Titanic callings particularly well. It\u2019s fine to give Scions access to Knacks and even Callings from this section that fit their concept and their parent\u2019s nature. Storyguides shouldn\u2019t hesitate to allow players to use this material on that basis.<br /> The Theoi and Tuatha possess many familial ties to their Titanic kin, while the Atua and Guarani might even be considered more Titan than God on the whole. Using these Callings and Knacks for themselves and their Scions is particularly appropriate.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T14:15:34-07:00","id":1505705,"title":"","content":"What does the Damage Convertion Knack do that normal first aid doesn't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T17:16:50-07:00","id":1505719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1505705#post1505705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does the Damage Convertion Knack do that normal first aid doesn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Heal Aggravated Damage (knacks are magical abilities)<br /> 2. Downgrade multiple Damage Conditions at a time (First Aid has to target an Injury Condition; Damage Conversion works on all the Conditions the target has at once)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T11:18:59-07:00","id":1506499,"title":"","content":"How many Calling dots is a Scion considered to have when buying Knacks from her Guide's Calling?<br /> <br /> Can a Sorcerer with a 3+ Guide buy Knacks from her Guide's Calling like a Scion? Does she benefit from the innate power of a Guide's or Relic's Purview? Can she use its Marvels?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T06:53:32-08:00","id":1547455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1506499#post1506499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many Calling dots is a Scion considered to have when buying Knacks from her Guide's Calling?<br /> <br /> <b>Can a Sorcerer with a 3+ Guide buy Knacks from her Guide's Calling like a Scion? Does she benefit from the innate power of a Guide's or Relic's Purview? Can she use its Marvels?</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The following is just my opinion:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>They can not buy Knacks as there is no listed cost of them for Sorcerers. They can benefit from Relics and Guides that grant them, but not buy them. Lost the Guide / Relic, lost the Knack.</li> <li>They would benefit from the Innate Power of the Purview, but no way to buy Boons. No listed cost of them for Sorcerers. They can benefit from Relics and Guides that grant Boons, but not buy them. Lost the Guide / Relic, lost the Purview and Boons.</li> <li>I would say No to Marvels. Not in character for Sorcerers.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-08-2025, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T07:02:33-08:00","id":1547456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scion 2ed p.66</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>YAMARAJA</b>,<br /> THE KING OF DEATH<br /> Aliases:<b> Imra, Yanluowang, Enma Dai-o, Yeomna<br /> Daewang, Shinje</b><br /> ....<br /> Since <b>Yamaraja </b>rules Naraka, many Asian peoples\u2019<br /> shared afterworld, <b>he is as much Sh\u00e9n, Kami, and Pala as he<br /> is Dev\u00e1.</b> Of all the Dev\u00e1 \u2014 indeed, of all the Gods, he is busiest<br /> and most stressed. His organizational skills and wise judg-<br /> ment make him invaluable to all these pantheons. <b>He wields<br /> the Purviews of Yoga, Tianming, Yidam, and Yaoyorozu-no-<br /> Kamigami in equal measures.</b>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It is incredible that you can have 4 different Scions of the same god, and each one having a different PSP, a one-man Band this god.<br /> <br /> Can a Scion get multiple PSP from Yamaraja? Or do you need to be God to have multiple PSP?\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-03T16:29:31-08:00","id":1547505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1547456#post1547456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is incredible that you can have 4 different Scions of the same god, and each one having a different PSP, a one-man Band this god.<br /> <br /> Can a Scion get multiple PSP from Yamaraja? Or do you need to be God to have multiple PSP?<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Yamaraja has access to all PSPs at the same time. This entity may have four more or less identical mantles, one for each Pantheon they belong to. So it depends for their Scions which mantle is the &quot;actual parent&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12016-echsenkoenig","name":"Echsenkoenig","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-12T08:01:21-07:00","id":1549189,"title":"","content":"Scion 2nd Ed<br /> God of War Kratos' Blades of Chaos<br /> Any idea how to stat these as Relic weapons?<br /> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28138-blackheart","name":"Blackheart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T09:03:18-07:00","id":1549671,"title":"","content":"Can you create new Mantle?<br /> If yes how do to create Mantle? <br /> And how many Mantle can a God have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","user":"Yumlum","date":".  More question 03-31-2025, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T23:51:51-07:00","id":1550141,"title":"","content":"I have a question concerning the Classical Amazon knacks in both Origin and Hero. They refer to a Warrior Knack called &quot;Armorbound&quot;, but that knack doesn't seem to exist in the list of Warrior Knacks. Is it there, and I'm just somehow missing it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26917-dmneaz","name":"dmneaz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T20:10:31-07:00","id":1550895,"title":"","content":"Probably a versioning error. Well Tempered on P. 113 Origin is the only Warrior Knack referencing armor. So I'd use that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","name":"SpanishInquisition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-27T19:33:17-07:00","id":1551322,"title":"","content":"does sorcerer keep up with scions in the long game? Like, how bad is power imbalance or is it nonexistent? I've been thinking of building one for a game my dm plans to play long term (hopefully up to and the end of apotheosis and wanted to know if it feels like you're left behind in the dust or not. I know they get some pretty cool stuff but from what I've seen doesn't inspire too much confidence. I might be missing something though since I'm new to the system","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28836-general-gratas","name":"General gratas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T20:08:24-08:00","id":1557630,"title":"","content":"Were the Titan Callings ever expanded upon for Demigod / God level of play? I haven't been able to find any information about them outside of Titanomachy, which only scaled them up to Hero level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T20:55:09-08:00","id":1557632,"title":"","content":"Do you have Titans Rising?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T21:00:46-08:00","id":1557634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1557632#post1557632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have Titans Rising?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not. Bought some other books for Christmas which had been on my wishlist for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T21:12:37-08:00","id":1557636,"title":"","content":"I haven't read it thoroughly; but it <i>does </i>flesh out Titans and Titanspawn further, and it won't surprise me if part of that is elaborating on the Titan Callings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T13:46:16-08:00","id":1557737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1557636#post1557636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read it thoroughly; but it <i>does </i>flesh out Titans and Titanspawn further, and it won't surprise me if part of that is elaborating on the Titan Callings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Checked it up on DriveThru, and that does seem to be the case.<br /> <br /> Course, I can't really be sure, because of writer's tendency to put a multi page mini-story in the book, before getting to actual mechanics.<br /> <br /> The advertisement does imply it's scaled up through each level of power (Origin, Hero, Demigod, God).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T07:12:48-08:00","id":1557801,"title":"","content":"How would I go about turning my character into a Kaiju that levels cities and devours their population?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T08:28:49-08:00","id":1557807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224340-ask-a-question-get-an-answer-scion-edition?p=1557801#post1557801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would I go about turning my character into a Kaiju that levels cities and devours their population?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on your character's Purviews and Callings, but one option could be the Beast Purview's &quot;Aspect of the Apex Predator&quot; Boon (found in Scion God on page 188, although it's theorically also available for Heroes and Demigods). The Destroyer and Monster Titanic Callings also have a number of Knacks that can help enable what you're looking for. If you own the two Dragon books, you could also play an Heir and see what you can do with Dragon Callings and Dragon Magic (the latter's basically the Dragon equivalent of Purviews, btw). The Dragon Companion book <i>literally</i> has legally distinct Godzilla as one of the available Dragon parents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}